  FT["MY-H1340"] = {"id":"MY-H1340","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 142/2025&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年地方政府（违法行为罚款了结）（纳闽联邦直辖区）附例","en":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025","orig":"LOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025","ms":"Undang-Undang Kecil Kerajaan Tempatan (Pengkompaunan Kesalahan) (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2025","vi":"Quy chế về Chính quyền địa phương (Xử lý vi phạm bằng phạt tiền) (Lãnh thổ Liên bang Labuan) năm 2025","th":"ข้อบัญญัติการปกครองส่วนท้องถิ่น (การระงับข้อหาด้วยค่าปรับ) (เขตการปกครองสหพันธ์ลาบวน) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Peraturan Daerah Pemerintahan Daerah (Penyelesaian Pelanggaran dengan Denda) (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) Tahun 2025"},"level":"law","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA142","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 7 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2025_P.U.(A)142-2025_LOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES) (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1340-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Undang-undang kecil ini bolehlah dinamakan Undang-Undang Kecil\n\nKerajaan Tempatan (Pengkompaunan Kesalahan) (Wilayah Persekutuan\n\nLabuan) 2025.\n\n(2) Undang-Undang Kecil ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 2 Mei 2025.\n\nKesalahan yang boleh dikompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. (1) Kesalahan yang dinyatakan dalam Jadual Pertama ditetapkan sebagai\n\nkesalahan yang boleh dikompaun.\n\n(2) Kesalahan yang boleh dikompaun itu boleh dikompaun dengan keizinan\n\nsecara bertulis Pendakwa Raya dalam Borang 1 Jadual Kedua.\n\nTatacara mengkompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. (1) Apabila menerima apa-apa maklumat atau aduan bahawa suatu kesalahan\n\nyang boleh dikompaun telah dilakukan, Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana\n\npegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan boleh, dengan\n\nkeizinan secara bertulis Pendakwa Raya yang disebut dalam perenggan 2(2),\n\nmengeluarkan suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun kesalahan itu dalam Borang 2\n\nJadual Kedua.\n\n(2) Suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun suatu kesalahan adalah sah bagi\n\ntempoh empat belas hari bermula dari tarikh tawaran itu diterima oleh orang yang\n\nkepadanya tawaran itu dibuat atau apa-apa tempoh lanjutan yang boleh diberikan oleh\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis\n\noleh Perbadanan Labuan, dan jika pembayaran penuh bagi jumlah yang ditawarkan itu\n\ndibuat pada atau sebelum habis tempoh empat belas hari atau apa-apa tempoh lanjutan\n\nyang diberikan itu, tiada prosiding selanjutnya boleh diambil terhadap orang yang telah\n\nmelakukan kesalahan itu.\n\nPenyetujuterimaan kompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Seseorang yang menyetuju terima suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun\n\nsuatu kesalahan yang boleh dikompaun hendaklah menyetuju terima tawaran itu\n\ndalam Borang 3 Jadual Kedua dan mengembalikan Borang 3 itu kepada\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis\n\noleh Perbadanan Labuan.\n\nPembayaran kompaun"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. (1) Jika suatu tawaran untuk mengkompaun suatu kesalahan disetuju terima\n\noleh orang yang kepadanya tawaran itu dibuat, dia hendaklah membayar\n\nkompaun itu—\n\n(a) secara tunai dan hendaklah diserahkan sendiri kepada\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa\n\nsecara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan ke alamat yang dinyatakan\n\ndalam Borang 2 Jadual Kedua;\n\n(b) melalui kiriman wang, wang pos, cek juruwang atau draf bank yang\n\ndipalang dengan perkataan \"Akaun Penerima Sahaja\" yang kena\n\ndibayar kepada Perbadanan Labuan dan hendaklah diserahkan sendiri\n\natau dihantar melalui pos berdaftar kepada Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif\n\natau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis oleh\n\nPerbadanan Labuan ke alamat yang dinyatakan dalam Borang 2\n\nJadual Kedua; atau\n\n(c) melalui kad kredit, kad debit, kad caj atau apa-apa bentuk pemindahan\n\nwang secara elektronik yang lain ke dalam akaun Perbadanan Labuan.\n\n(2) Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara\n\nbertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan hendaklah mengeluarkan suatu resit rasmi bagi\n\ntiap-tiap pembayaran yang diterima di bawah perenggan (1) kepada orang yang\n\nkepadanya tawaran untuk mengkompaun kesalahan itu dibuat.\n\n(3) Suatu resit rasmi yang dikeluarkan di bawah perenggan (2) hendaklah\n\ntermasuk apa-apa resit elektronik jika pembayaran dibuat melalui pemindahan wang\n\nsecara elektronik.\n\nJumlah wang yang dikehendaki dipungut"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. Jumlah wang yang dikehendaki dipungut oleh Perbadanan Labuan bagi\n\nmengkompaun suatu kesalahan di bawah Akta atau suatu kesalahan yang dinyatakan\n\ndalam Jadual Pertama hendaklah tidak melebihi amaun maksima bagi denda yang\n\ndiperuntukkan dalam Akta bagi kesalahan itu.\n\nPendakwaan boleh dimulakan jika tiada pembayaran dibuat"}},{"id":"MY-H1340-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"ms":"7. Jika tiada pembayaran bagi kompaun yang ditawarkan itu dibuat dalam\n\ntempoh yang dinyatakan dalam perenggan 3(2), pendakwaan boleh dimulakan tanpa\n\nnotis selanjutnya.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n[Perenggan 2(1) dan Undang-Undang Kecil 6]\n\nKESALAHAN YANG BOLEH DIKOMPAUN\n\nKesalahan yang berikut ditetapkan sebagai kesalahan yang boleh dikompaun:\n\n(a) kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah Akta Kerajaan Tempatan 1976\n\n[Akta 171], sebagaimana yang diperluas dan diubah suai melalui Perintah\n\nWilayah Persekutuan Labuan (Pemerluasan dan Ubah Suaian Akta Kerajaan\n\nTempatan 1976) 2010 [P.U. (A) 439/2010] seperti yang berikut:\n\n(i) seksyen 69;\n\n(ii) seksyen 70;\n\n(iii) seksyen 74;\n\n(iv) subseksyen 75(2);\n\n(v) subseksyen 76(2);\n\n(vi) subseksyen 77(4);\n\n(vii) subseksyen 77(7);\n\n(viii) seksyen 78;\n\n(ix) subseksyen 82(5);\n\n(x) subseksyen 95(1);\n\n(xi) subseksyen 95(2);\n\n(xii) subseksyen 97(2);\n\n(xiii) subseksyen 99(2);\n\n(xiv) subseksyen 107(6);\n\n(xv) seksyen 109;\n\n(xvi) subseksyen 111(2);\n\n(xvii) seksyen 112;\n\n(xviii) seksyen 119;\n\n(xix) subseksyen 140(2);\n\n(xx) subseksyen 160(6); dan\n\n(xxi) subseksyen 161(6);\n\n(b) kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil Pelesenan Tred,\n\nPerniagaan dan Perindustrian (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016\n\n[P.U. (A) 231/2016] seperti yang berikut:\n\n(i) perenggan 13(3);\n\n(ii) perenggan 15(3);\n\n(iii) perenggan 16(2);\n\n(iv) perenggan 17(2);\n\n(v) perenggan 19(4);\n\n(vi) perenggan 20(2);\n\n(vii) perenggan 21(2);\n\n(viii) perenggan 22(2);\n\n(ix) perenggan 23(2);\n\n(x) perenggan 25(2);\n\n(xi) perenggan 26(2);\n\n(xii) perenggan 27(3);\n\n(xiii) perenggan 27(4);\n\n(xiv) perenggan 28(3);\n\n(xv) perenggan 28(4);\n\n(xvi) perenggan 29(3);\n\n(xvii) perenggan 30(2);\n\n(xviii) perenggan 31(2);\n\n(xix) perenggan 33(2);\n\n(xx) perenggan 34(2); dan\n\n(xxi) perenggan 35(3);\n\n(c) kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil Pelesenan Pasar\n\n(Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016 [P.U. (A) 256/2016] seperti yang berikut:\n\n(i) perenggan 16(3);\n\n(ii) perenggan 18(6);\n\n(iii) perenggan 20(3);\n\n(iv) perenggan 21(2);\n\n(v) perenggan 22(2);\n\n(vi) perenggan 23(2);\n\n(vii) perenggan 24(3);\n\n(viii) perenggan 26(3);\n\n(ix) perenggan 27(2);\n\n(x) perenggan 28(2);\n\n(xi) perenggan 30(2);\n\n(xii) perenggan 31(4);\n\n(xiii) perenggan 32(4);\n\n(xiv) perenggan 33(2);\n\n(xv) perenggan 34(5);\n\n(xvi) perenggan 35(2);\n\n(xvii) perenggan 36(2);\n\n(xviii) perenggan 37(2);\n\n(xix) perenggan 38(2);\n\n(xx) perenggan 39(2);\n\n(xxi) perenggan 40(2);\n\n(xxii) perenggan 41(2);\n\n(xxiii) perenggan 42(4);\n\n(xxiv) perenggan 43(3);\n\n(xxv) perenggan 44(2);\n\n(xxvi) perenggan 45(2); dan\n\n(xxvii) perenggan 46(2);\n\n(d) kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil Pelesenan Penjaja\n\n(Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016 [P.U. (A) 344/2016] seperti yang berikut:\n\n(i) perenggan 10(2);\n\n(ii) perenggan 14(2);\n\n(iii) perenggan 15(4);\n\n(iv) perenggan 15(6);\n\n(v) perenggan 16(3);\n\n(vi) perenggan 18(6);\n\n(vii) perenggan 19(4);\n\n(viii) perenggan 20(4);\n\n(ix) perenggan 21(6);\n\n(x) perenggan 23(4);\n\n(xi) perenggan 24(3);\n\n(xii) perenggan 25(2);\n\n(xiii) perenggan 26(4);\n\n(xiv) perenggan 27(2);\n\n(xv) perenggan 28(2);\n\n(xvi) perenggan 29(2);\n\n(xvii) perenggan 30(2);\n\n(xviii) perenggan 31(4);\n\n(xix) perenggan 32(2);\n\n(xx) perenggan 33(3);\n\n(xxi) perenggan 34(3);\n\n(xxii) perenggan 35(2);\n\n(xxiii) perenggan 37(2); dan\n\n(xxiv) perenggan 38(2);\n\n(e) kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil Pelesenan Petempatan\n\nMakanan (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016 [P.U. (A) 363/2016] seperti\n\nyang berikut:\n\n(i) perenggan 15(5);\n\n(ii) perenggan 16(2);\n\n(iii) perenggan 18(2);\n\n(iv) perenggan 19(5);\n\n(v) perenggan 20(5);\n\n(vi) perenggan 21(2);\n\n(vii) perenggan 22(2);\n\n(viii) perenggan 23(4);\n\n(ix) perenggan 23(6);\n\n(x) perenggan 24(2);\n\n(xi) perenggan 25(2);\n\n(xii) perenggan 26(2);\n\n(xiii) perenggan 27(6);\n\n(xiv) perenggan 28(1);\n\n(xv) perenggan 28(3);\n\n(xvi) perenggan 29(2);\n\n(xvii) perenggan 30(3);\n\n(xviii) perenggan 31(2);\n\n(xix) perenggan 32(2);\n\n(xx) perenggan 33(4);\n\n(xxi) perenggan 34(2);\n\n(xxii) perenggan 35(3);\n\n(xxiii) perenggan 35(4);\n\n(xxiv) perenggan 36(2);\n\n(xxv) perenggan 37(3); dan\n\n(xxvi) perenggan 38(2).\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\nBORANG 1\n\n[Perenggan 2(2)]\n\nAKTA KERAJAAN TEMPATAN 1976\n\nUNDANG-UNDANG KECIL KERAJAAN TEMPATAN (PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN)\n\n(WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN LABUAN) 2025\n\nKEIZINAN UNTUK MENGKOMPAUN KESALAHAN\n\nPADA menjalankan kuasa yang diberikan oleh Fasal (3) Perkara 145\n\nPerlembagaan Persekutuan dan subseksyen 376(3) Kanun Tatacara Jenayah [Akta 593],\n\nsaya ………………………………………………………………… (nama) dengan ini memberi keizinan\n\nuntuk mengkompaun ……..…………………………………………………………………….. (nama orang\n\nyang kepadanya tawaran kompaun itu dibuat) bagi kesalahan yang dilakukan di bawah\n\n………………………………………………………………………………… yang dikatakan telah dilakukan\n\npada ……………………………………….. (tarikh) di …………………………………………………. (tempat).\n\n Tarikh:\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n Pendakwa Raya/\n\n Timbalan Pendakwa Raya\n\nBORANG 2\n\n[Perenggan 3(1) dan 5(1)]\n\nAKTA KERAJAAN TEMPATAN 1976\n\nUNDANG-UNDANG KECIL KERAJAAN TEMPATAN (PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN)\n\n(WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN LABUAN) 2025\n\nTAWARAN UNTUK MENGKOMPAUN KESALAHAN\n\nNombor rujukan : ………………………………………\n\nTarikh : ………………………………………\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif/\n\nmana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan\n\nPerbadanan Labuan\n\nPeti Surat 81245\n\n87022 Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan\n\nKepada:\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n*Tuan/Puan,\n\nSuatu penyiasatan telah dijalankan terhadap anda ………………………………………………………\n\n(nyatakan nama *individu/syarikat/perniagaan/badan lain dan nombor pendaftaran,\n\njika ada) dan anda didapati telah melakukan kesalahan di bawah Akta Kerajaan\n\nTempatan 1976 [Akta 171], sebagaimana yang diperluas dan diubah suai melalui\n\nPerintah Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan (Pemerluasan dan Ubah Suaian Akta Kerajaan\n\nTempatan 1976) 2010 [P.U. (A) 439/2010]/undang-undang kecil yang dibuat di bawah\n\nAkta dengan butir-butir yang berikut:\n\n(a) *peruntukan Akta/undang-undang kecil yang berkaitan:\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n(b) tarikh : ………………………………………\n\n(c) masa : ………………………………………\n\n(d) tempat : ………………………………………\n\n(e) **butir-butir kesalahan:\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n2. Menurut Fasal (3) Perkara 145 Perlembagaan Persekutuan dan\n\nsubseksyen 376(3) Kanun Tatacara Jenayah [Akta 593], dengan keizinan secara bertulis\n\nPendakwa Raya, anda ditawarkan suatu kompaun bagi kesalahan yang dinyatakan\n\ndi atas bagi jumlah wang sebanyak RM………………. (..………..……………… (dalam perkataan)\n\nringgit sahaja).\n\n3. Sekiranya tawaran untuk mengkompaun ini disetuju terima, pembayaran\n\nhendaklah dibuat—\n\n(a) secara tunai dan hendaklah diserahkan sendiri kepada\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif atau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa\n\nsecara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan ke alamat Perbadanan Labuan,\n\nPeti Surat 81245, 87022 Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan;\n\n(b) melalui *kiriman wang/wang pos/cek juruwang/draf bank yang\n\ndipalang dengan perkataan \"Akaun Penerima Sahaja\" yang kena\n\ndibayar kepada Perbadanan Labuan dan hendaklah diserahkan sendiri\n\natau dihantar melalui pos berdaftar kepada Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif\n\natau mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis oleh\n\nPerbadanan Labuan ke alamat Perbadanan Labuan, Peti Surat 81245,\n\n87022 Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan; atau\n\n(c) melalui kad kredit, kad debit, kad caj atau apa-apa bentuk pemindahan\n\nwang secara elektronik yang lain ke dalam akaun Perbadanan Labuan.\n\n4. Suatu resit rasmi akan dikeluarkan apabila pembayaran kompaun itu diterima.\n\n5. Tawaran untuk mengkompaun ini sah bagi tempoh empat belas hari bermula\n\ndari tarikh tawaran ini diterima oleh anda.\n\n6. Jika tiada bayaran diterima dalam tempoh yang disebut dalam perenggan 5,\n\npendakwaan bagi kesalahan itu boleh dimulakan terhadap anda\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………. (nyatakan\n\nnama *individu/syarikat/perniagaan/badan lain dan nombor pendaftaran, jika ada)\n\ntanpa notis selanjutnya.\n\n…………………………………………………………………\n\n Ketua Pegawai Eksekutif/\n\n mana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa\n\n secara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan\n\n________________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\n*Potong mana-mana yang tidak berkenaan\n\n**Nyatakan butiran dan gunakan lampiran jika perlu\n\nBORANG 3\n\n[Perenggan 4]\n\nAKTA KERAJAAN TEMPATAN 1976\n\nUNDANG-UNDANG KECIL KERAJAAN TEMPATAN (PENGKOMPAUNAN KESALAHAN)\n\n(WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN LABUAN) 2025\n\nPENYETUJUTERIMAAN TAWARAN UNTUK MENGKOMPAUN KESALAHAN\n\nKepada:\n\nKetua Pegawai Eksekutif/\n\nmana-mana pegawai yang diberi kuasa secara bertulis oleh Perbadanan Labuan\n\nPerbadanan Labuan\n\nPeti Surat 81245\n\n87022 Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan\n\n*Tuan/Puan,\n\nSaya merujuk kepada Tawaran untuk Mengkompaun Kesalahan dengan nombor\n\nrujukan ……………………………………… bertarikh …………………………………….\n\n2. Saya mengaku bahawa saya telah melakukan kesalahan ini dan saya menerima\n\ntawaran untuk mengkompaun itu dan disertakan bersama-sama ini pembayaran\n\n*wang tunai/kiriman wang/wang pos/cek juruwang/draf bank no. ……………………………\n\ndipalang dengan perkataan \"Akaun Penerima Sahaja\" yang kena dibayar kepada\n\nPerbadanan Labuan/bukti pembayaran melalui *kad kredit/kad debit/\n\nkad caj/pemindahan wang secara elektronik sebanyak RM……………………..\n\n(…………………………………… (dalam perkataan) ringgit sahaja) sebagai penyelesaian\n\npenuh bagi jumlah wang yang dinyatakan dalam perenggan 2 Tawaran untuk\n\nMengkompaun Kesalahan.\n\nTandatangan : ……………………………………………………\n\n**Nama (huruf besar) : ……………………………………………………\n\n*No. Kad Pengenalan/No. Pasport : ……………………………………………………\n\n***Untuk dan bagi pihak : ……………………………………………………\n\n (nama *syarikat/perniagaan/badan lain)\n\n***Jawatan : ……………………………………………………\n\n***Meterai syarikat/cap perniagaan atau badan lain : ……………………………………………….\n\n***No. Pendaftaran Syarikat/No. Lesen/No. Permit : ……………………………………………….\n\nAlamat : …………………………………………………………………………….\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\nTarikh : ……………………………………………………\n\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\n*Potong mana-mana yang tidak berkenaan\n\n**Nama orang yang kepadanya tawaran untuk mengkompaun itu dibuat atau nama pengarah bagi pihak\n\nsyarikat/perniagaan/badan lain\n\n***Dalam hal jika tawaran untuk mengkompaun itu dibuat kepada syarikat/perniagaan/badan lain\n\nDibuat 22 April 2025\n\n[PL/PUU/100-1/4 Jld. 6 (7); PN(PU2)328]\n\nTAN SRI DATUK SERI PANGLIMA ANIFAH BIN AMAN @ HANIFF AMMAN\n\nPengerusi Perbadanan Labuan\n\nDisahkan 29 April 2025\n\n[KWP(S):24/PUU/698/1/2/21; PN(PU2)328]\n\n DATUK SERI DR. ZALIHA BINTI MUSTAFA\n\nMenteri di Jabatan Perdana Menteri\n\n (Wilayah Persekutuan)\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 102(t) of the Local Government\n\nAct 1976 [Act 171], as extended and modified by the Federal Territory of Labuan\n\n(Extension and Modification of Local Government Act 1976) Order 2010\n\n[P.U. (A) 439/2010]), the Perbadanan Labuan makes, and pursuant to section 103\n\nof the Act, the Minister confirms, the following by-laws:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) These by-laws may be cited as the Local Government (Compounding\n\nof Offences) (Federal Territory of Labuan) By-Laws 2025.\n\n(2) These By-Laws come into operation on 2 May 2025.\n\nCompoundable offences\n\n2. (1) The offences specified in the First Schedule are prescribed to be\n\ncompoundable offences.\n\n(2) The compoundable offences may be compounded with the consent in writing\n\nof the Public Prosecutor in Form 1 of the Second Schedule.\n\nProcedure for compounding\n\n3. (1) Upon receipt of any information or complaint that a compoundable offence\n\nhas been committed, the Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing\n\nby the Perbadanan Labuan may, with the consent in writing of the Public Prosecutor\n\nreferred to in paragraph 2(2), issue an offer to compound the offence in Form 2\n\nof the Second Schedule.\n\n(2) An offer to compound an offence shall be valid for a period of fourteen days\n\nstarting from the date the offer is received by the person to whom offer is made or such\n\nextended period as the Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing\n\nby the Perbadanan Labuan may grant, and if full payment of the sum offered is made on\n\nor before the expiry of the period of fourteen days or such extended period granted,\n\nno further proceedings shall be taken against the person who committed such offence.\n\nAcceptance of compound\n\n4. A person who accepts an offer to compound a compoundable offence\n\nshall accept the offer in Form 3 of the Second Schedule and return the Form 3 to the\n\nChief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan.\n\nPayment of compound\n\n5. (1) If an offer to compound an offence is accepted by the person to whom\n\nthe offer is made, the person shall pay the compound—\n\n(a) in cash and shall be delivered personally to the Chief Executive Officer\n\nor any officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan to the\n\naddress specified in Form 2 of the Second Schedule;\n\n(b) by money order, postal order, cashier's cheque or bank draft\n\ncrossed with the words \"Account Payee Only\" made payable\n\nto the Perbadanan Labuan and shall be delivered personally or sent\n\nby registered post to the Chief Executive Officer or any officer\n\nauthorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan to the address\n\nspecified in Form 2 of the Second Schedule; or\n\n(c) through credit card, debit card, charge card or any other forms\n\nof electronic fund transfer into the Perbadanan Labuan's account.\n\n(2) The Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing\n\nby the Perbadanan Labuan shall issue an official receipt for every payment received\n\nunder paragraph (1) to the person to whom the offer to compound an offence is made.\n\n(3) An official receipt issued under paragraph (2) shall include any electronic\n\nreceipt if the payment is made through an electronic fund transfer.\n\nSum of money to be collected\n\n6. The sum of money to be collected by the Perbadanan Labuan for\n\ncompounding an offence under the Act or an offence specified in the First Schedule\n\nshall not exceed the maximum amount of fine as provided in the Act for the offence.\n\nProsecution may be instituted if no payment made\n\n7. If no payment of the compound offered is made within the period\n\nspecified in paragraph 3(2), prosecution may be instituted without further notice.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n[Paragraph 2(1) and By-Law 6]\n\nCOMPOUNDABLE OFFENCES\n\nThe following offences are prescribed to be compoundable offences:\n\n(a) the offences committed under the Local Government Act 1976 [Act 171],\n\nas extended and modified by the Federal Territory of Labuan (Extension and\n\nModification of Local Government Act 1976) Order 2010 [P.U. (A) 439/2010]\n\nas follows:\n\n(i) section 69;\n\n(ii) section 70;\n\n(iii) section 74;\n\n(iv) subsection 75(2);\n\n(v) subsection 76(2);\n\n(vi) subsection 77(4);\n\n(vii) subsection 77(7);\n\n(viii) section 78;\n\n(ix) subsection 82(5);\n\n(x) subsection 95(1);\n\n(xi) subsection 95(2);\n\n(xii) subsection 97(2);\n\n(xiii) subsection 99(2);\n\n(xiv) subsection 107(6);\n\n(xv) section 109;\n\n(xvi) subsection 111(2);\n\n(xvii) section 112;\n\n(xviii) section 119;\n\n(xix) subsection 140(2);\n\n(xx) subsection 160(6); and\n\n(xxi) subsection 161(6);\n\n(b) the offences committed under the Licensing of Trades, Businesses and Industries\n\n(Federal Territory of Labuan) By-Laws 2016 [P.U. (A) 231/2016] as follows:\n\n(i) paragraph 13(3);\n\n(ii) paragraph 15(3);\n\n(iii) paragraph 16(2);\n\n(iv) paragraph 17(2);\n\n(v) paragraph 19(4);\n\n(vi) paragraph 20(2);\n\n(vii) paragraph 21(2);\n\n(viii) paragraph 22(2);\n\n(ix) paragraph 23(2);\n\n(x) paragraph 25(2);\n\n(xi) paragraph 26(2);\n\n(xii) paragraph 27(3);\n\n(xiii) paragraph 27(4);\n\n(xiv) paragraph 28(3);\n\n(xv) paragraph 28(4);\n\n(xvi) paragraph 29(3);\n\n(xvii) paragraph 30(2);\n\n(xviii) paragraph 31(2);\n\n(xix) paragraph 33(2);\n\n(xx) paragraph 34(2); and\n\n(xxi) paragraph 35(3);\n\n(c) the offences committed under the Licensing of Markets (Federal Territory\n\nof Labuan) By-Laws 2016 [P.U. (A) 256/2016] as follows:\n\n(i) paragraph 16(3);\n\n(ii) paragraph 18(6);\n\n(iii) paragraph 20(3);\n\n(iv) paragraph 21(2);\n\n(v) paragraph 22(2);\n\n(vi) paragraph 23(2);\n\n(vii) paragraph 24(3);\n\n(viii) paragraph 26(3);\n\n(ix) paragraph 27(2);\n\n(x) paragraph 28(2);\n\n(xi) paragraph 30(2);\n\n(xii) paragraph 31(4);\n\n(xiii) paragraph 32(4);\n\n(xiv) paragraph 33(2);\n\n(xv) paragraph 34(5);\n\n(xvi) paragraph 35(2);\n\n(xvii) paragraph 36(2);\n\n(xviii) paragraph 37(2);\n\n(xix) paragraph 38(2);\n\n(xx) paragraph 39(2);\n\n(xxi) paragraph 40(2);\n\n(xxii) paragraph 41(2);\n\n(xxiii) paragraph 42(4);\n\n(xxiv) paragraph 43(3);\n\n(xxv) paragraph 44(2);\n\n(xxvi) paragraph 45(2); and\n\n(xxvii) paragraph 46(2);\n\n(d) the offences committed under the Licensing of Hawkers (Federal Territory\n\nof Labuan) By-Laws 2016 [P.U. (A) 344/2016] as follows:\n\n(i) paragraph 10(2);\n\n(ii) paragraph 14(2);\n\n(iii) paragraph 15(4);\n\n(iv) paragraph 15(6);\n\n(v) paragraph 16(3);\n\n(vi) paragraph 18(6);\n\n(vii) paragraph 19(4);\n\n(viii) paragraph 20(4);\n\n(ix) paragraph 21(6);\n\n(x) paragraph 23(4);\n\n(xi) paragraph 24(3);\n\n(xii) paragraph 25(2);\n\n(xiii) paragraph 26(4);\n\n(xiv) paragraph 27(2);\n\n(xv) paragraph 28(2);\n\n(xvi) paragraph 29(2);\n\n(xvii) paragraph 30(2);\n\n(xviii) paragraph 31(4);\n\n(xix) paragraph 32(2);\n\n(xx) paragraph 33(3);\n\n(xxi) paragraph 34(3);\n\n(xxii) paragraph 35(2);\n\n(xxiii) paragraph 37(2); and\n\n(xxiv) paragraph 38(2);\n\n(e) the offences committed under the Licensing of Food Establishments\n\n(Federal Territory of Labuan) By-Laws 2016 [P.U. (A) 363/2016] as follows:\n\n(i) paragraph 15(5);\n\n(ii) paragraph 16(2);\n\n(iii) paragraph 18(2);\n\n(iv) paragraph 19(5);\n\n(v) paragraph 20(5);\n\n(vi) paragraph 21(2);\n\n(vii) paragraph 22(2);\n\n(viii) paragraph 23(4);\n\n(ix) paragraph 23(6);\n\n(x) paragraph 24(2);\n\n(xi) paragraph 25(2);\n\n(xii) paragraph 26(2);\n\n(xiii) paragraph 27(6);\n\n(xiv) paragraph 28(1);\n\n(xv) paragraph 28(3);\n\n(xvi) paragraph 29(2);\n\n(xvii) paragraph 30(3);\n\n(xviii) paragraph 31(2);\n\n(xix) paragraph 32(2);\n\n(xx) paragraph 33(4);\n\n(xxi) paragraph 34(2);\n\n(xxii) paragraph 35(3);\n\n(xxiii) paragraph 35(4);\n\n(xxiv) paragraph 36(2);\n\n(xxv) paragraph 37(3); and\n\n(xxvi) paragraph 38(2).\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nFORM 1\n\n[Paragraph 2(2)]\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025\n\nCONSENT TO COMPOUND OFFENCE\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by Clause (3) of Article 145 of the\n\nFederal Constitution and subsection 376(3) of the Criminal Procedure Code [Act 593],\n\nI ……………………………………………………………………………………… (name) hereby give consent\n\nto compound ……………………………………………………………………………… (name of the person\n\nto whom the compound offer is made) for the offence committed under\n\n…………………………………………………………………… which is said to have been committed on\n\n………………………………………………… (date) at ………………...…………………………………… (place).\n\n Date:\n\n…………………………………………………………\n\n Public Prosecutor/\n\n Deputy Public Prosecutor\n\nFORM 2\n\n[Paragraphs 3(1) and 5(1)]\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025\n\nOFFER TO COMPOUND OFFENCE\n\nReference number : ………………………………………\n\nDate : ………………………………………\n\nThe Chief Executive Officer/\n\nany officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan\n\nPerbadanan Labuan\n\nP.O. Box 81245\n\n87022 Federal Territory of Labuan\n\nTo:\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n……………………………………………………\n\n*Sir/Madam,\n\nAn investigation has been conducted against you …………………………………………………………\n\n(state name of *individual/company/business/other body and the registration number,\n\nif any) and you are found to have committed an offence under the Local Government\n\nAct 1976 [Act 171], as extended and modified by the Federal Territory of Labuan\n\n(Extension and Modification of Local Government Act 1976) Order 2010\n\n[P.U. (A) 439/2010]/by-laws made under the Act with the following particulars:\n\n(a) *relevant provisions of the Act/by-laws:\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n(b) date : ………………………………………\n\n(c) time : ………………………………………\n\n(d) place : ………………………………………\n\n(e) **particulars of offence:\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………………………\n\n2. Pursuant to Clause (3) of Article 145 of the Federal Constitution and\n\nsubsection 376(3) of the Criminal Procedure Code [Act 593], with the consent in writing\n\nof the Public Prosecutor, you are offered a compound for the offence stated above for\n\nthe sum of RM……………………….… (……………………………………………………………… (in words)\n\nringgit only).\n\n3. If the offer to compound is accepted, payment shall be made—\n\n(a) in cash and shall be delivered personally to the Chief Executive Officer or\n\nany officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan to the address\n\nat Perbadanan Labuan, P.O. Box 81245, 87022 Federal Territory of Labuan;\n\n(b) by *money order/postal order/cashier's cheque/bank draft crossed with\n\nthe words \"Account Payee Only\" made payable to the Perbadanan Labuan\n\nand shall be delivered personally or sent by registered post to\n\nthe Chief Executive Officer or any officer authorized in writing\n\nby the Perbadanan Labuan to the address at Perbadanan Labuan,\n\nP.O. Box 81245, 87022 Federal Territory of Labuan; or\n\n(c) through credit card, debit card, charge card or any other forms of electronic\n\nfund transfer into the Perbadanan Labuan's account.\n\n4. An official receipt shall be issued on receipt of payment of the compound.\n\n5. This offer to compound shall be valid for a period of fourteen days starting from\n\nthe date the offer is received by you.\n\n6. If there is no payment received within the period referred to in paragraph 5,\n\nthe prosecution for the offence may be instituted against you\n\n……………………………………………………………………………………………………………… (state name\n\nof *individual/company/business/other body and the registration number, if any)\n\nwithout further notice.\n\n……………………………………………………………\n\n Chief Executive Officer/\n\n any officer authorized\n\n in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan\n\n________________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\n*Delete whichever is inapplicable\n\n**State details and use appendix if necessary\n\nFORM 3\n\n[Paragraph 4]\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT (COMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES)\n\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2025\n\nACCEPTANCE OF OFFER TO COMPOUND OFFENCE\n\nTo:\n\nThe Chief Executive Officer/\n\nany officer authorized in writing by the Perbadanan Labuan\n\nPerbadanan Labuan\n\nP.O. Box 81245\n\n87022 Federal Territory of Labuan\n\n*Sir/Madam,\n\nI refer to the Offer to Compound Offence bearing the reference number\n\n……………………………………… dated ……………………………………….\n\n2. I admit that I have committed this offence and I accept the offer to compound\n\nand enclosed herewith is the payment in *cash/money order/postal order/cashier's\n\ncheque/banker's draft no. ……………………………………… crossed with the words\n\n\"Account Payee Only\" made payable to the Perbadanan Labuan/proof of payment\n\nthrough *credit card/debit card/charge card/electronic fund transfer for the sum of\n\nRM………………..…… (…………………………………… (in words) ringgit only) as full settlement\n\nof the sum stipulated in paragraph 2 of the Offer to Compound Offence.\n\nSignature : ……………………………………………………\n\n**Name (in capital letter) : ……………………………………………………\n\n*Identification No./Passport No. : ……………………………………………………\n\n***For and on behalf : ……………………………………………………\n\n (name of *company/business/other body)\n\n***Designation : ……………………………………………………\n\n***Company seal/stamp of business or other body : ……………………………………………\n\n***Company Registration No./Licence No./Permit No. : ……………………………………………\n\nAddress : ...…………………………………………………………………………\n\n………………………………………………………………………………………………..…………………………………\n\n…………………………………………………………..………………………………………………………………………\n\nDate : …………………………………………………\n\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\n*Delete whichever is inapplicable\n\n**Name of the person to whom the offer to compound is made or name of the director on behalf\n\nof company/business/other body\n\n***In the case where the offer to compound is made to the company/business/other body\n\nMade 22 April 2025\n\n[PL/PUU/100-1/4 Jld. 6 (7); PN(PU2)328]\n\nTAN SRI DATUK SERI PANGLIMA ANIFAH BIN AMAN @ HANIFF AMMAN\n\nChairman of the Perbadanan Labuan\n\nConfirmed 29 April 2025\n\n[KWP(S):24/PUU/698/1/2/21; PN(PU2)328]\n\n DATUK SERI DR. ZALIHA BINTI MUSTAFA\n\n Minister in the Prime Minister's Department\n\n (Federal Territories)"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1341"] = {"id":"MY-H1341","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 142/2026&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年供应管制（禁止买卖受管制物品）（RON95汽油）条例","en":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (PROHIBITION OF SALE AND PURCHASE OF CONTROLLED ARTICLE) (RON 95 PETROL) REGULATIONS 2026","orig":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (PROHIBITION OF SALE AND PURCHASE OF CONTROLLED ARTICLE) (RON 95 PETROL) REGULATIONS 2026","ms":"Peraturan Kawalan Bekalan (Larangan Penjualan dan Pembelian Barang Kawalan) (Petrol RON 95) 2026","vi":"Quy định về Kiểm soát nguồn cung (Cấm bán và mua hàng hóa bị kiểm soát) (Xăng RON 95) năm 2026","th":"ข้อบังคับการควบคุมเสบียง (การห้ามขายและซื้อสิ่งของควบคุม) (น้ำมันเบนซิน RON 95) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Peraturan Pengendalian Persediaan (Larangan Penjualan dan Pembelian Barang Terkendali) (Bensin RON 95) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA142","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 5 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)142-2026_CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (PROHIBITION OF SALE AND PURCHASE OF CONTROLLED ARTICLE) (RON 95 PETROL) RE.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1341-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\n\nKawalan Bekalan (Larangan Penjualan dan Pembelian Barang Kawalan)\n\n(Petrol RON 95) 2026.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 April 2026.\n\nTafsiran"}},{"id":"MY-H1341-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Dalam Peraturan-Peraturan ini—\n\n\"kenderaan motor asing\" ertinya suatu kenderaan motor yang didaftarkan oleh\n\npihak berkuasa yang sepatutnya di suatu negara asing;\n\n\"petrol RON 95\" ertinya produk yang diperoleh daripada petroleum dalam bentuk\n\nminyak dengan nombor oktana penyelidikan 95.\n\nLarangan penjualan petrol RON 95"}},{"id":"MY-H1341-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. (1) Tiada seorang pun boleh menjual petrol RON 95 kepada mana-mana orang\n\nbagi kegunaan kenderaan motor asing tanpa kebenaran bertulis Pengawal.\n\n(2) Mana-mana orang yang melanggar subperaturan (1) melakukan\n\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nLarangan pembelian petrol RON 95"}},{"id":"MY-H1341-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. (1) Tertakluk kepada subperaturan (2), tiada seorang pun boleh membeli\n\npetrol RON 95 bagi kegunaan kenderaan motor asing tanpa kebenaran bertulis Pengawal.\n\n(2) Subperaturan (1) tidak terpakai bagi pembelian petrol RON 95 di tempat\n\nyang dinyatakan dalam Jadual, dengan syarat bahawa—\n\n(a) petrol RON 95 yang dibeli daripada tempat tersebut tidak boleh\n\ndiangkut bagi apa-apa urus niaga selanjutnya yang lain; dan\n\n(b) petrol RON 95 itu hendaklah dibeli dalam harga pasaran.\n\n(3) Mana-mana orang yang melanggar peraturan ini melakukan\n\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPermohonan bagi kebenaran bertulis"}},{"id":"MY-H1341-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. (1) Permohonan bagi kebenaran bertulis untuk menjual atau membeli\n\npetrol RON 95 bagi kegunaan kenderaan motor asing hendaklah dibuat kepada Pengawal\n\nmengikut cara yang ditentukan oleh Pengawal.\n\n(2) Pengawal boleh memberi kebenaran bertulis tertakluk kepada syarat yang\n\ndifikirkannya patut untuk mengelakkan penyalahgunaan kebenaran bertulis.\n\n(3) Pengawal boleh, pada bila-bila masa selepas pemberian kebenaran\n\nbertulis, menambah, memotong atau mengubah syarat yang baginya kebenaran bertulis\n\nitu tertakluk.\n\n(4) Pengawal boleh membatalkan suatu kebenaran bertulis pada bila-bila\n\nmasa jika orang yang kepadanya kebenaran bertulis itu diberi melanggar syarat\n\nkebenaran bertulis itu.\n\nJADUAL\n\n(1)\n\nBil.\n\n(2)\n\nTempat\n\n1. Semua stesen minyak di Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan\n\n2. Semua stesen minyak di Pulau Langkawi, Kedah\n\n3. Stesen minyak Double Endorse Sdn. Bhd. yang terletak di—\n\n(a) Lot 37 & 38, Kawasan Perindustrian Kampung Kolam,\n\nPadang Besar Utara, 02100 Padang Besar, Perlis; dan\n\n(b) Lot 54 & 55, Kawasan Perindustrian Bukit Kayu Hitam,\n\n06050 Bukit Kayu Hitam, Kedah\n\n4. Stesen minyak Rafliesia YNWN Development Sdn. Bhd. yang\n\nterletak di Lot 9141, GM 975, Mukim Titi Tinggi,\n\nKampung Wang Kelian, 02200 Kaki Bukit, Perlis\n\n5. Stesen minyak An Marketing Trading Sdn. Bhd. yang terletak\n\ndi Lot 4019, Bandar Bukit Kayu Hitam, 06050 Bukit Kayu\n\nHitam, Kedah\n\nDibuat27 Mac 2026\n\n[KPDN.600-9/3/12(25); PN(PU2)188/JLD.14]\n\nDATUK ARMIZAN BIN MOHD ALI\n\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri dan Kos Sara Hidup\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES ACT 1961\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES (PROHIBITION OF SALE AND\n\nPURCHASE OF CONTROLLED ARTICLE) (RON 95 PETROL) REGULATIONS 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraphs 6(2)(a), (c) and (n) of the\n\nControl of Supplies Act 1961 [Act 122], the Minister makes the following regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Control of Supplies\n\n(Prohibition of Sale and Purchase of Controlled Article) (RON 95 Petrol)\n\nRegulations 2026.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 1 April 2026.\n\nInterpretation\n\n2. In these Regulations—\n\n\"foreign motor vehicle\" means a motor vehicle which is registered by the proper\n\nauthority of a foreign country;\n\n\"RON 95 petrol\" means a product derived from petroleum in the form of oil with\n\na research octane number of 95.\n\nProhibition of sale of RON 95 petrol\n\n3. (1) No person shall sell RON 95 petrol to any person for use in a foreign motor\n\nvehicle without the written permission of the Controller.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes subregulation (1) commits an offence.\n\nProhibition of purchase of RON 95 Petrol\n\n4. (1) Subject to subregulation (2), no person shall purchase RON 95 petrol for\n\nuse in a foreign motor vehicle without the written permission of the Controller.\n\n(2) Subregulation (1) shall not apply to the purchase of RON 95 petrol at the\n\nplaces as specified in the Schedule, provided that—\n\n(a) the RON 95 petrol purchased from those places shall not be\n\ntransported for any further dealings; and\n\n(b) the RON 95 petrol is purchased at the market price.\n\n(3) Any person who contravenes this regulation commits an offence.\n\nApplication for written permission\n\n5. (1) An application for a written permission to sell or purchase RON 95 petrol\n\nfor use in a foreign motor vehicle shall be made to the Controller in the manner\n\nas may be determined by the Controller.\n\n(2) The Controller may grant a written permission subject to such condition\n\nas he thinks fit to prevent the misuse of the written permission.\n\n(3) The Controller may, at any time after the grant of written permission,\n\nadd to, delete or vary the condition to which the written permission is subject.\n\n(4) The Controller may revoke a written permission at any time if the person\n\nto whom the written permission is granted contravenes the condition of the\n\nwritten permission.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n(1)\n\nNo.\n\n(2)\n\nPlace\n\n1. All petrol stations in the Federal Territory of Labuan\n\n2. All petrol stations on Langkawi Island, Kedah\n\n3. Petrol stations of Double Endorse Sdn. Bhd. situated at—\n\n(a) Lot 37 & 38, Kawasan Perindustrian Kampung Kolam,\n\nPadang Besar Utara, 02100 Padang Besar, Perlis; and\n\n(b) Lot 54 & 55, Kawasan Perindustrian Bukit Kayu Hitam,\n\n06050 Bukit Kayu Hitam, Kedah\n\n4. Petrol station of Rafliesia YNWN Development Sdn. Bhd.\n\nsituated at Lot 9141, GM 975, Mukim Titi Tinggi,\n\nKampung Wang Kelian, 02200 Kaki Bukit, Perlis\n\n5. Petrol station of An Marketing Trading Sdn. Bhd. situated at\n\nLot 4019, Bandar Bukit Kayu Hitam, 06050 Bukit Kayu\n\nHitam, Kedah\n\nMade 27 March 2026\n\n[KPDN.600-9/3/12(25); PN(PU2)188/JLD.14]\n\nDATUK ARMIZAN BIN MOHD ALI\n\nMinister of Domestic Trade and Cost of Living"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1342"] = {"id":"MY-H1342","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/1970&status=","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1970年紧急状态（基本权力）第32号条例","en":"Emergency (Essential Powers) Ordinance No. 32, 1970","orig":"Emergency (Essential Powers) Ordinance No. 32, 1970","vi":"Pháp lệnh số 32 về Tình trạng khẩn cấp (Các quyền hạn thiết yếu) năm 1970","th":"พระราชกำหนด ฉบับที่ 32 ภาวะฉุกเฉิน (อำนาจจำเป็น) ค.ศ. 1970","id":"Ordinansi Nomor 32 Keadaan Darurat (Kewenangan Pokok) Tahun 1970","ms":"Ordinan Bil. 32 Darurat (Kuasa Penting) 1970"},"level":"decree","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1970","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 4 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\1970_P.U.(A)143-1970_Emergency (Essential Powers) Ordinance No. 32, 1970.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1342-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. This Ordinance may be cited as the Emergency (Essen- Citation.\ntial Powers) Ordinance No. 32, 1970.\nr@paey7e"}},{"id":"MY-H1342-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. (1) Section 7 of the Emergency (Essential Powers)\" b mption\nOrdinance No. 1, 1969 is hereby repealed and the following oleae\nprovisions shall have effect.                                 elections.\n\n(2) Elections to the Dewan Ra‘ayat and Legislative\nAssembly in respect of Sarawak and elections to the Dewan\nRa‘ayat in respect of Sabah\nSelatan shall, subject to the following sections of this\nOrdinance, be recommenced.\n\nPUA 204/70"}},{"id":"MY-H1342-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"3. Notwithstanding anything contained in any written law— writs,\n(a) save as provided in paragraph (5), all writs, notices valid excep;\n\nand other documents issued or made in ‘relation in certain\n\nto the elections to the Dewan Ra‘ayat and Legis- soning days\nlative Assembly in respect of Sarawak and the and retaking\n\nelections to the Dewan Ra‘ayat in respect of of polls in\nSabah                                   D cases.\n\nd/PUCA 204/70 —\n\nP\n\n\"(1) Subsection (1) of section 7 of the\nEmergency (Essential Powers) Ordinance No. 1,\n1969 is hereby repealed in so far as it applies\nto Sabah and Sarawak; and the following pro-\nvisions shall have effect.\";                PUCA) 204/70\n\nTe\n\nP.U. (A) 143.                                       814\n\neee\n\nDeath or\ndisqualifica-\ntion of\ncandidates.\n\nshall continue to remain valid and to have force\nand effect subject to the following provisions of\nthis Ordinance;\n\n(b) in respect of the elections recommenced by virtue\nof this Ordinance, the poll shall be taken on such\nday or days as may be determined by the Election\nCommission;\n\n(c) in any constituency where the poll had commenced\nbut not completed immediately before the coming\ninto force of section 7 of the Emergency (Essen-\ntial Powers) Ordinance No. 1, 1969, the poll shall\nbe retaken and all documents  referred to in\nregulation 24 (1) of the Elections (Conduct of\nElections) (Sabah and Sarawak) Regulations, 1968\nand regulation 11 of the Elections (Postal Voting)\n(Sabah and Sarawak) Regulations, 1968 and all\nthe contents of the sealed boxes referred to in\nregulation 24 (2) of the Elections (Conduct of\nElections) (Sabah and Sarawak) Regulations, 1968\nand regulation 13 of the Elections (Postal Voting)\n(Sabah and Sarawak) Regulations, 1968 in respect\nthereof shall be destroyed;\n\n(d) if at any time after the elections are recommenced\nunder this Ordinance, it is shown to the satis-\nfaction of the Election Commission that in any\nconstituency or any polling station, owing to any\ncause whatsoever, the poll cannot be taken or has\nnot been taken or has been taken but cannot be\ncompleted on the date or dates determined under\nparagraph (b), the Election Commission shall, by\nnotice published in the constituency or local area\nfor which the polling station is designated as the\ncase may be, suspend the poll and appoint fresh\ndate or dates for the poll to be taken or to be\ncompleted in such manner as may be directed by\nthe Election Commission."}},{"id":"MY-H1342-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"4. (1) In the case where before the poll has commenced by\nvirtue of this Ordinance in any constituency and one of the\ncandidates nominated dies or becomes disqualified for being\na member of the Dewan Ra‘ayat or the Legislative Assembly\nof a State as the case may be, the Election Commission\nshall, upon being satisfied  with such fact, countermand\nthe notice of the poll and shall appoint by notice published\nin the Gazette and in such newspapers as it thinks fit a fresh\ndate or dates for the election.\n\n(2) In every such case all proceedings with reference to\nthe election shall be commenced afresh under the relevant\nprovisions of the law relating to elections provided that no\n\nfresh nomination shall be necessary in the case of a qualified\ncandidate who stood nominated at the time of the counter-\nmand of the poll.\n\nin sub-section (2) soliciting for\nbehalf of any candidate or any\npolitical party or the political or other opinion entertained\nor supposed to be entertained by such candidate or such\npolitical party or the use or display of any slogan for any\ncandidate or any political party shall be prohibited.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding sub-section (1)}—\n\n(a) symbols or pictures of the candidates or symbols of\npolitical parties  participating in the  election\ntogether with the words \"Vote For\" may be used\nor displayed in accordance with the provisions\nof any law relating to election offences;\n\nuency where all proceedings with\nhe election are commenced afresh\nunder section 4 (2) and where a new candidate or\ncandidates have been nominated, each of the\ncandidates in such constituency may subject to\nsub-section (3) issue and distribute a manifesto\ncontaining the picture of the candidate and his\nsymbol or the symbol of a political party setting\nout the aims and objectives of the candidate or\nparty:\n\nProvided that such manifesto shall not contain\nmatters which are likely to lead to the breach of\nthe peace or public order or likely to promote\nfeelings of ill-will and hostility between the\ndifferent races or classes of the population :\n\nProvided further that the distribution of such\nmanifesto shall be limited to one issue only, and\nshall be confined  within the limits of  such\n\nconstituency.\n\n(3) The Minister charged with the responsibility for Home\nAffairs may in any particular case prohibit the distribution\nof any manifesto in the interest of public security.\n\n(4) Any person who contravenes sub-section (1) and any\nperson who distributes or causes to be distributed any mani-\nfesto which has been prohibited under sub-section (3) shall\nbe guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years or to\na fine not exceeding ten thousand dollars or to both such\n\nimprisonment and fine.\n\n5, (1) Except as provided\nvotes or support for or on\n\n(b) in any constit\nreference to t\n\nP.U. (A) 143.\n\nCo a—\n\nRestrictions\non election\ncampaign.\n\nP.U. (A) 143.                          816\n\nSm tai\n\n(5) For the purpose of this section, \"soliciting for votes\nor support\" includes—\n\n(a) convening or organising or assisting in convening\nor organising any public meeting, procession or\ndemonstration with a view to or for the purpose\nof gaining votes or support;\n\n(b) interviewing members of the public for the purpose\nof the election except as provided for in section 26A\n\nAct 5.                of the Election Offences Act, 1954;\n\n(c) writing, printing, distributing or  displaying or\ncausing to be written, printed, distributed or\ndisplayed any appeal in favour of or against any\ncandidate or political party except as provided in\nsub-section (2);\n\n(d) damaging, altering or removing any posters, papers\n|                              or banners which had been displayed under sub-\n|                      section (2) (a);\n|                         (e) using any musical instrument or loud speaker in or\n\nupon any premises, vessels, animals, motor cars,\n. |                          trucks or other vehicles as or for the purpose of\npolitical propaganda;\n(f) making statements of a political nature to the press;\n(g) incurring any expenditure for any of the matters\nspecified above.\n\nmeragam aan\neet etal te DADA AAA\n\nie to in forceXshall apply to anything done or omitted to be done\n\"          elections. in respect of elections in Sabah and  Sarawak and—the—\nKin Sabah and sensti                            recommenced by virtue of\nSarawak    this Ordinance.\n\n1m 204/76 -   (2) This Ordinance shall cease to have effect as soon as\n<1/ PU(A) 254/70 the elections recommenced by virtue of this Ordinance shall\nhave been completed save in respect of anything done or\n\nomitted to be done under this Ordinance or under any other\n\nlaw relating to elections.\n\nPromulgated at Istana Negara, Kuala Lumpur, on 10th\nday of May, 1970.           |        !\n[MGN (PA) R. 21.11/Jld. 4.1\n\nTUANKU ISMAIL NASIRUDDIN SHAH,\n\n|\n|           Operation 6, (1) Subject to this Ordinance, all laws relating to elections\n\n|                                                      Yang di-Pertuan Agong\n\nDI-CHETAK DI-JABATAN CHETAK KERAJAAN, KUALA LUMPUR, OLEH MOHAMED BIN ABDULLAH, A.M.N.,\nPEMANGKU PENCHETAK KERAJAAN\n\nesa"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1343"] = {"id":"MY-H1343","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2014&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2014年反洗钱与反恐怖主义融资（附表二修正）令","en":"ANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING AND ANTI-TERRORISM FINANCING (AMENDMENT OF SECOND SCHEDULE) ORDER 2014","orig":"ANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING AND ANTI-TERRORISM FINANCING (AMENDMENT OF SECOND SCHEDULE) ORDER 2014","ms":"Perintah Anti Pengubahan Wang Haram dan Anti Pembiayaan Keganasan (Pindaan Jadual Kedua) 2014","vi":"Lệnh về Chống rửa tiền và chống tài trợ khủng bố (Sửa đổi Phụ lục thứ hai) năm 2014","th":"คำสั่งการต่อต้านการฟอกเงินและการต่อต้านการจัดหาเงินทุนแก่การก่อการร้าย (การแก้ไขภาคผนวกที่สอง) ค.ศ. 2014","id":"Perintah Anti Pencucian Uang dan Anti Pendanaan Terorisme (Perubahan Lampiran Kedua) Tahun 2014"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2014","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\2014_P.U.(A)143-2014_ANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING AND ANTI-TERRORISM FINANCING (AMENDMENT OF SECOND SCHEDULE) ORDER 2014.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1343-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pencegahan Pengubahan Wang\nHaram dan Pencegahan Pembiayaan Keganasan (Pindaan Jadual Kedua) 2014.\n\nPindaan Jadual Kedua"}},{"id":"MY-H1343-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Akta Pencegahan Pengubahan Wang Haram dan Pencegahan Pembiayaan\nKeganasan 2001 dipinda dalam Jadual Kedua—\n\n (a)  dengan memasukkan selepas kepala \"Akta Kawalan Pertukaran Wang\n1953 [ Akta 17 ]\" dan butiran yang berhubungan dengannya kepala dan\nbutiran yang berikut:\n\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nAkta Eksais 1976 [Akta 176]\nSeksyen 71 Membuat pernyataan salah dan\nmemalsukan dokumen\nSeksyen 73 Keengganan untuk menjawab\nsoalan atau memberi maklumat\npalsu\nSeksyen 74 Mengelak duti eksais dan\npengilangan haram barang yang\nberduti \";\n\"\n\n (b) dengan memasukkan  selepas kepala \"Akta Suruhanjaya Pencegahan\nRasuah Malaysia 2009 [ Akta 694 ]\" dan butiran yang berhubungan\ndengannya kepala dan butiran yang berikut :\n\n(c) dengan memasukkan selepas kepala \"Akta Pemberi Pinjam Wang 1951\n[Akta 400 ]\" dan butiran yang berhubungan dengannya kepala dan\nbutiran yang berikut:\n\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nAkta Lembaga Minyak Sawit Malaysia 1998 [Akta 582]\nSeksyen 67 Maklumat palsu\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nPeraturan-Peraturan Lembaga Minyak Sawit Malaysia\n(Perlesenan) 2005\n [P.U. (A) 516/2005]\nPeraturan 5 Larangan terhadap mengeluarkan\natau menjual, dsb., tanpa lesen\nPeraturan 21 Pematuhan syarat yang dikenakan\natas lesen\nPeraturan 40 Larangan terhadap pencurian\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nAkta Perniagaan Perkhidmatan Wang 2011 [Akta 731]\nSeksyen 4 Larangan menjalankan perniagaan\nperkhidmatan wang\n\"\n\"\n\";\n\";\n\n(d) dengan memasukkan  selepas kepala \"Kanun Keseksaan [ Akta 574]\" dan\nbutiran yang berhubungan dengannya kepala dan butiran yang berikut:\n\n(e) dengan memasukkan selepas kepala \"Akta Perindustrian Sekuriti 1983\n[Akta 280]\" dan butiran yang berhubungan dengannya ke pala dan butiran\nyang berikut:\n\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nAkta Cukai Perkhidmatan 1975 [Akta 151]\nSeksyen 29 Kegagalan untuk patuh dengan notis,\ndsb.\nSeksyen 32 Pengelakkan cukai perkhidmatan\n\nDibuat 15 Mei 2014\n[BNM. JUN 1125/3603; PN(PU2)622/XIV]\n\n                 DATO' SERI HAJI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\n                     Menteri Kewangan Kedua\n\nKesalahan Perihalan*\nAkta Cukai Jualan 1972 [Akta 64]\nSeksyen 43 Kegagalan untuk patuh dengan notis, dsb.\nSeksyen 43A Pengelakkan cukai jualan\n\"\n\".\n\"; dan\n\"\n\nANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING AND ANTI-TERRORISM FINANCING ACT 2001\n\nANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING AND ANTI-TERRORISM FINANCING (AMENDMENT OF\nSECOND SCHEDULE) ORDER 2014\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 85 of the Anti-Money Laundering and\nAnti-Terrorism Financing Act 2001 [Act 613], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1344"] = {"id":"MY-H1344","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2015&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2015年供应管制（管制物品）（第3号）令","en":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 3) ORDER 2015","orig":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 3) ORDER 2015","ms":"Perintah Kawalan Bekalan (Barang Kawalan) (Bilangan 3) 2015","vi":"Lệnh về Kiểm soát nguồn cung (Hàng hóa được kiểm soát) (số 3) năm 2015","th":"คำสั่งการควบคุมเสบียง (สิ่งของควบคุม) (ฉบับที่ 3) ค.ศ. 2015","id":"Perintah Pengendalian Persediaan (Barang yang Dikendalikan) (Nomor 3) Tahun 2015"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2015","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2015_P.U.(A)143-2015_CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 3) ORDER 2015.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1344-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kawalan Bekalan\n\n(Barang-Barang Kawalan) (No. 3) 2015.\n\nBarang-barang kawalan"}},{"id":"MY-H1344-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Barang-barang yang dinyatakan dalam Jadual diisytiharkan sebagai\n\nbarang-barang kawalan bagi tempoh dari 4 Julai 2015 hingga 9 Jun 2016.\n\nJADUAL\n\nBARANG-BARANG KAWALAN\n\n1. Semua jenis mentega\n\n2. Semua jenis keju\n\n3. Semua jenis marjerin\n\n4. Semua jenis minuman kotak atau botol\n\n5. Semua jenis serbuk penaik dan esen membuat kuih-muih dan konfeksi\n\n6. Jeli dan agar-agar\n\n7. Daging dan jeroan mentah (segar atau dijeruk)\n\n8. Itik dan burung-burung lain, tidak termasuk ayam\n\n9. Telur dan telur diawet\n\n10. Buah-buahan mentah yang diimport (segar atau dijeruk)\n\n11. Bawang besar dan bawang merah\n\n12. Bawang putih\n\n13. Cili kering\n\n14. Lada hitam dan semua jenis rempah\n\n15. Kelapa (sebiji atau yang diparut)\n\n16. Semua jenis kacang pea dan kacang\n\n17. Semua jenis kacang tanah\n\n18. Cendawan dan kulat\n\n19. Minyak sapi\n\n20. Asam jawa\n\n21. Makanan laut (dikeringkan atau dijeruk)\n\n22. Tepung beras\n\n23. Tepung jagung\n\n24. Tepung beras pulut\n\n25. Ubi kentang\n\nDibuat 1 Julai 2015\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/VIII]\n\nDATO' SRI HASAN BIN MALEK\n\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri,\n\n Koperasi dan Kepenggunaan\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES ACT 1961\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 3) ORDER 2015\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 5 of the Control of Supplies Act 1961\n\n[Act 122], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Control of Supplies (Controlled Articles)\n\n(No. 3) Order 2015.\n\nControlled articles\n\n2. The articles specified in the Schedule are declared to be controlled articles for\n\nthe period from 4 July 2015 to 9 June 2016.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nCONTROLLED ARTICLES\n\n1. All types of butter\n\n2. All types of cheese\n\n3. All types of margarine\n\n4. All types of packed or bottled drinks\n\n5. All types of baking powder and essences for making cakes and\n\nconfectionery\n\n6. Jelly and agar-agar\n\n7. Raw meat and offal (fresh or preserved)\n\n8. Duck and other birds, excluding chicken\n\n9. Eggs and preserved eggs\n\n10. Raw imported fruits (fresh or preserved)\n\n11. Onion and shallot\n\n12. Garlic\n\n13. Dried chillies\n\n14. Black pepper and all types of spices\n\n15. Coconuts (whole or scraped)\n\n16. All types of peas and beans\n\n17. All types of groundnuts\n\n18. Mushroom and fungi\n\n19. Ghee\n\n20. Tamarind\n\n21. Seafood (dried or preserved)\n\n22. Rice flour\n\n23. Corn flour\n\n24. Glutinous rice flour\n\n25. Potatoes\n\nMade 1 July 2015\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/VIII]\n\nDATO' SRI HASAN BIN MALEK\n\nMinister of Domestic Trade,\n\nCo-operatives and Consumerism"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1345"] = {"id":"MY-H1345","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2016&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2016年价格管制与反暴利（管制商品标价）（第3号）令","en":"PRICE CONTROL AND ANTI-PROFITEERING (PRICE MARKING OF PRICE-CONTROLLED GOODS) (NO. 3) ORDER 2016","orig":"PRICE CONTROL AND ANTI-PROFITEERING (PRICE MARKING OF PRICE-CONTROLLED GOODS) (NO. 3) ORDER 2016","ms":"Perintah Kawalan Harga dan Anti-Pencatutan (Penandaan Harga Barang Kawalan Harga) (Bilangan 3) 2016","vi":"Lệnh về Kiểm soát giá và chống trục lợi (Niêm yết giá hàng hóa thuộc diện kiểm soát giá) (số 3) năm 2016","th":"คำสั่งการควบคุมราคาและการต่อต้านการฉวยโอกาส (การแสดงราคาสินค้าควบคุมราคา) (ฉบับที่ 3) ค.ศ. 2016","id":"Perintah Pengendalian Harga dan Anti-Pencatutan (Penandaan Harga Barang yang Dikendalikan Harganya) (Nomor 3) Tahun 2016"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2016","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2016_P.U.(A)143-2016_PRICE CONTROL AND ANTI-PROFITEERING (PRICE MARKING OF PRICE-CONTROLLED GOODS) (NO. 3) ORDER 201.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1345-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kawalan Harga dan\nAntipencatutan (Penandaan Harga Barangan Harga Terkawal) (No. 3) 2016.\n\n (2)  Perintah ini b erkuat kuasa bagi tempoh dari 25 Mei 2016\nhingga 3 Jun 2016.\n\nPenandaan harga"}},{"id":"MY-H1345-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. (1) Mana-mana orang yang   menjual atau menawarkan untuk menjual\napa-apa barangan harga terkawal yang disiarkan dalam Perintah Kawalan Harga dan\nAntipencatutan (Penent uan H arga Maksimum) (No. 3 ) 2016  [P.U. (A) 141/2016]\nhendaklah meletakkan label berwarna merah jambu yang menunjukkan harga bagi\nsetiap unit atau setiap unit timbangan, nama yang memerihalkan barangan  harga\nterkawal itu dan gred atau kualiti, jika ada, bagi barangan harga terkawal itu.\n\n (2) Mana-mana orang yang tidak mematuhi subperenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan dan boleh, apabila disabitkan—\n\n(a) jika orang itu suatu pertubuhan perbadanan, didenda\ntidak melebihi dua puluh ribu ringgit dan, bagi kesalahan kali\nyang kedua atau yang berikutnya, didenda tidak melebihi\nlima puluh ribu ringgit; atau\n\n(b) jika orang itu bukan suatu pertubuhan perbadanan, didenda\ntidak melebihi sepuluh ribu ringgit dan, bagi kesalahan kali\nyang kedua atau yang berikutnya, didenda tidak melebihi\ndua puluh ribu ringgit.\n\nDibuat  19 Mei 2016\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)26/0.5001/1 Jld.12; PN(PU2)695/XII]\n\nDATO' SERI HAMZAH BIN ZAINUDIN\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri,\nKoperasi dan Kepenggunaan\n\nPRICE CONTROL AND ANTI-PROFITEERING ACT 2011\n\nPRICE CONTROL AND ANTI-PROFITEERING\n(PRICE MARKING OF PRICE-CONTROLLED GOODS) (NO. 3) ORDER 2016\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 10 of the\nPrice Control and Anti -Profiteering Act 2011 [ Act 723 ], the Minister\nmakes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
