  FT["MY-H1349"] = {"id":"MY-H1349","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2021&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2021年司法委任委员会（高级法院法官遴选程序与委任方法）（修正）条例","en":"JUDICIAL APPOINTMENTS COMMISSION (SELECTION PROCESS AND METHOD OF APPOINTMENT OF JUDGES OF THE SUPERIOR COURTS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2021","orig":"JUDICIAL APPOINTMENTS COMMISSION (SELECTION PROCESS AND METHOD OF APPOINTMENT OF JUDGES OF THE SUPERIOR COURTS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2021","ms":"Peraturan Suruhanjaya Pelantikan Kehakiman (Proses Pemilihan dan Kaedah Pelantikan Hakim Mahkamah Atasan) (Pindaan) 2021","vi":"Quy định về Ủy ban Bổ nhiệm Tư pháp (Quy trình tuyển chọn và phương thức bổ nhiệm thẩm phán các tòa án cấp cao) (Sửa đổi) năm 2021","th":"ข้อบังคับคณะกรรมการแต่งตั้งตุลาการ (กระบวนการคัดเลือกและวิธีการแต่งตั้งผู้พิพากษาศาลชั้นสูง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2021","id":"Peraturan Komisi Pengangkatan Yudisial (Proses Seleksi dan Metode Pengangkatan Hakim Pengadilan Tinggi) (Perubahan) Tahun 2021"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2021","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\2021_P.U.(A)143-2021_JUDICIAL APPOINTMENTS COMMISSION (SELECTION PROCESS AND METHOD OF APPOINTMENT OF JUDGES OF THE.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1349-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\nSuruhanjaya Pelantikan Kehakiman (Proses Pemilihan dan Kaedah Pelantikan\nHakim-Hakim Mahkamah Atasan) (Pindaan) 2021.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 30 Mac 2021.\n\nPindaan peraturan 8"}},{"id":"MY-H1349-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Suruhanjaya Pelantikan Kehakiman (Proses Pemilihan dan\nKaedah Pelantikan Hakim -Hakim Mahkamah Atasan) 2009 [P.U. (A) 209/2009 ] dipinda\ndalam subperaturan 8(1)—\n\n(a) dalam perenggan (c), dengan memotong perkataan \"dan\" di hujung\nperenggan itu;\n\n(b) dalam perenggan (d), dengan menggantikan noktah di hujung perenggan\nitu dengan perkataan \"; dan\"; dan\n\n(c) dengan memasukkan selepas perenggan (d) perenggan yang berikut:\n\n\"(e) Lembaga Hasil Dalam Negeri Malaysia.\".\n\nDibuat 15 Mac 2021\n[SPK(s).600-2/1/4(1); PN(PU2)680/II]\n\nTAN SRI DATO' HAJI MAHIADDIN BIN MD. YASIN\nPerdana Menteri\n\nJUDICIAL APPOINTMENTS ACT 2009\n\nJUDICIAL APPOINTMENTS COMMISSION\n(SELECTION PROCESS AND METHOD OF APPOINTMENT OF JUDGES OF THE\nSUPERIOR COURTS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2021\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 30 of the\nJudicial Appointments Commission Act 2009 [ Act 695 ], the Prime Minister, on the\nrecommendation of the Commission, makes the following regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H135"] = {"id":"MY-H135","coverage":"partial","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=100&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":36,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1949年信托公司法","en":"TRUST COMPANIES ACT 1949","orig":"TRUST COMPANIES ACT 1949","vi":"Luật về Công ty tín thác năm 1949","th":"พระราชบัญญัติบริษัททรัสต์ ค.ศ. 1949","id":"Undang-Undang Perusahaan Perwalian Tahun 1949","ms":"Akta Syarikat Amanah 1949"},"level":"law","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT100","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1949","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 38 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\1949_100_TRUST COMPANIES ACT 1949.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H135-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. This Ordinance may be cited as the Trust Short title.\n\nCompanies Ordinance, 1949."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. In this Ordinance, unless the context otherwise Interpreta-\nrequires—                                       hon.\n\n\"the Companies Ordinance'? means the Companies 8-8. Ord.\nNo. 42 of\n\nOrdinance, 1940, of the Straits Settlements as 1940.\nextended to apply throughout the Federation by the M.U, Ord.\nCompanies Ordinance, 1946;                       1946.\n\nApplication\nby company\nto be regis-\ntered as a\ntrust\ncompany.\n\nIssue of\ncertificate.\n\n9             No. 88 or 1949.\n\n\"the Court'? means the High Court or any Judge\nthereof in all cases where proceedings are taken in\nthe High Court, and a Sessions Court in all cases\nwhere proceedings are taken in a Sessions Court;\n\n\"the Registrar'? means the Registrar of Companies;\n\n\"trust company'? means a company registered as a\ntrust company under this Ordinance.\n\nREGISTRATION OF TRUST COMPANY."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"3. Any public company incorporated in the\nFederation may apply to the Registrar to be registered\nas a trust company, provided that—\n\n(a) the objects of the company are restricted\nto some or all of the objects set out in\nsection 8 of this Ordinance;\n\n(b) the authorised capital of the company is not\nless than five hundred thousand dollars\ndivided into shares of not less than ten\ndollars each;                                   |\n\n(c) at least one-half of the amount of every share\nissued by the company remains unpaid and\nis not liable to be called up, except in the\nevent and for the purpose of the winding\nup or dissolution of the company;\n\n(d) the board of directors has been duly appointed\nin accordance with the articles of associa-\ntion of the company;\n\n(e) at least ,one hundred and fifty thousand\ndollars of the authorised capital has been\nbona fide paid up;\n\n(f) the company has deposited with the\nAccountant-General securities to be\napproved by the Financial Secretary to the\nvalue of one hundred thousand dollars; and\n\n(7) the company is able to meet its obligations,\napart from its liability to its shareholders,\nwithout taking into account the securities\nso deposited with the Accountant-General."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"4. (1) On receipt of an application under section 3\nof this Ordinance, the Registrar shall make such\nenquiry as he deems necessary, and if satisfied that\nall the requirements of the said section 3 have been\ncomplied with, shall register the company applying for\nregistration in the register prescribed by section 6 of\nthis Ordinance and issue to the company a, certificate\nthat it is registered as a trust company, and thereupon\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                             3\n\nthe company shall be invested with all the powers,\nprivileges' and immunities conferred, and shall be\nsubject to all the liabilities imposed, by this Ordinance.\n(2) Notice of the issue of such certificate shall be\npublished by the Registrar in the Gazette for four\nconsecutive weeks next following the issue.\n\n(3) If the Registrar is not satisfied that all the\nrequirements of section 3 of this Ordinance, have been\n\ncomplied with, he shall refuse to register the company\n\nas a trust company :\n\nProvided that the company may appeal from such\nrefusal to the High Commissioner in Council, whose\ndecision shall be final.\n\n_ 5. (1) Any public company incorporated in the\nColony and registered in the Federation under Part X\nof the Companies Ordinance which obtains from the\nRegistrar a declaration that he is satisfied—\n\n(a) that it is registered as a trust company in the\nColony under any law for the time being in\nforce in the Colony relating to the regis-\ntration of trust companies; and\n\n(b) that, in accordance with such law, it has\ndeposited with the Accountant-General of\nthe Colony securities to the value of at least\none hundred thousand dollars,\n\nshall be entitled to apply to the Registrar for and\nobtain registration as a trust company in the\nFederation in accordance with section 4 of this\nOrdinance and may thereupon carry on the business of\na trust company in the Federation in accordance with\nthe provisions of this Ordinance so long as it remains\nregistered as a trust company in the Colony and\nmaintains such deposit as aforesaid :\n\nProvided that where the Registrar is of opinion\nthat, by reason of the amount of the gross liabilities\nof any such company in the Federation, additional\nsecurity ought to be furnished by that company, he\nmay order the company to make a deposit with the\nAccountant-General in the manner and subject to the\nappeal provided by sub-section (2) of section 7 of this\nOrdinance, and, upon such deposit being made, the\nsame shall be subject to all the provisions of this\nOrdinance relating to deposits.\n\n(2) This section shall have effect only if and so long\nas reciprocal provisions are contained in the law of the\nColony relating to trust companies.\n\nRegistration\nof company\nincorporated\nin the\nColony as a\ntrust\ncompany.\n\nRegister of\ntrust\ncompanies\nto be kept.\n\nDeposit to\n\nbe held as *\n\nsecurity.\n\nObjects.\n\nTrustee.\n\n4             No. 33 or 1949."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"6. There shall be kept in the office of the Registrar\na register, to be called the \"Register of Trust\nCompanies' in which shall be entered the names of all\ntrust companies registered under this Ordinance,\ntogether with such other particulars as the Registrar\nmay think necessary.\n\nDEPOSIT BY TRUST COMPANIES."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"en":"7. (1) From the time of the issue to any company of\na certificate under section 4 of this Ordinance, the\nsecurities deposited by the company with the\nAccountant-General under section 3 of this Ordinance\nshall be held by the Accountant-General as security\nfor the depositors and creditors of the company and\nfor the faithful execution of all trusts which may\nbe accepted by or imposed upon the company and for\nits obligations generally.\n\n(2) If at any time, by reason of the decline in value\nof any securities so held by the Accountant-General\nor of the increase of the gross liabilities of any trust\ncompany, the Registrar is of opinion that additional\nsecurity ought to be furnished by a trust company, he\nmay order the company to make, within a period to\nbe stated in the order, a further deposit of a specified\nvalue with the Accountant-General :\n\nProvided that the company may appeal from such\norder to the High Commissioner in Council, whose\ndecision shall be final.                                .\n\n(3) Any trust company may, from time to\ntime, with the approval of the Financial Secretary,\nsubstitute other securities for all or any of the securities\ndeposited. by it with the Accountant-General.\n\n(4) The interest accruing due on the securities\ndeposited shall be paid to the company.\n\nOBJECTS OF TRUST COMPANIES."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"en":"8. (1) The objects of a trust company may be any\nor all of, but shall not exceed, the following :\n\n(a) to accept and execute the offices of executor,\nadministrator, trustee, receiver, receiver\nand manager, assignee, liquidator, guar-\ndian of the property of an infant, commit-\ntee of the estate of a mentally disordered\nperson or other like office of a fiduciary\nnature;\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                             5\n\n(6) to act as attorney or agent for the collection,\nreceipt and payment of money, and for\nwinding up estates, and for the sale\nor purchase of any movable or immovable\nproperty ;\n\n(c) to act as agent for the management and\ncontrol of movable and immovable property\nfor and on behalf of the owners thereof,\nor for or on behalf of executors, admini-\nstrators or trustees;\n\n(d) to act as investing and financial agent for and\non behalf of executors, administrators and\ntrustees or any other persons whatsoever,\nand to receive money in trust for invest-\nment ‘and to allow interest thereon until\ninvested; and to undertake for and on\nbehalf of executors, administrators and\ntrustees or any other persons whatsoever\nthe negotiation of loans of all descriptions\nand the procuring and lending of money on\nthe security of any description of property,\nimmovable or movable, or without taking\nany security on such terms as may be\narranged, and to advance and lend moneys\nto protect any estate, trust or property\nentrusted to the company as aforesaid and\nto charge interest upon any such advances :\n\nProvided that nothing herein contained\nshall be held either to restrict or extend\nthe powers of the company as trustee\nor agent under the terms of any trust or\nagency that may be conferred upon it;\n\n(e) to take securities of such nature as are deemed\nexpedient for any moneys owing to the\ncompany ;\n\n(7) to be the custodian on such terms as are agreed\nupon of any moneys, securities, jewellery,\nplate or other valuable property and of\npapers, documents, deeds, wills, debentures\nand other evidence of title or indebtedness;\n\n(9) to receive and manage any sinking, redemp-\ntion, guarantee or any other special fund\nor deposit and to act as agent for counter-\nsigning, registering or otherwise ascertain-\ning and certifying to the genuineness\n\nAgency.\n\nManaging\nagent.\n\nInvesting\nagent, etc.\n\nSecurities\nfor debts.\n\nCustodian.\n\nSinking .\nfunds, etc.\n\nTo hold\nland for\ncompany's\nuse.\n\nTo hold\nother land.\n\nTo deposit\nand invest\nthe moneys\nof the\ncompany in\nauthorised\n\ninvestments.\n\nTo borrow\nmoneys.\n\nRemunera-\ntion.\n\nTo contri-\nbute to\ncharities.\n\nNo. 33 oF 1949.\n\nof any issue of shares, stocks, bonds,\ndebentures or other securities for money of\nany Government, municipal or other\ncorporate body or of any association,\nwhether incorporated or not, duly authoris-\ned to issue and make such issue and to hold\nany such securities as agent or trustee, and\nto act generally as agent for any such\nGovernment, municipal or corporate body\nor association;\n\n(k) to acquire and hold immovable property for\n' the actual use and occupation of the\ncompany or of any of its officers and\nservants; and to erect, construct, enlarge,\nalter and maintain any buildings necessary\nor convenient for the said purpose; and to\nsell or otherwise dispose of any such\nimmovable property if not required for the\n\nsaid purposes;\n\n(4) to hold land which, having been mortgaged or.\ncharged to the company, is acquired. by it\nfor the protection of its investments; and,\nfrom time to time, sell, mortgage, charge,\nlease or otherwise dispose thereof;\n\n(j) to deposit the moneys of the company not\nimmediately required with any bank or\nbanks at interest until such moneys can be\nmore permanently invested, and to invest\nthe moneys of the company in accordarice\nwith the provisions of section 18 of this\nOrdinance;\n\n(k) to borrow moneys, and secure the repayment\nthereof with interest, in accordance with\nthe provisions of section 20 of this\nOrdinance;\n\n(I) to receive and collect such remuneration for\nits services as is agreed upon or as fixed\nor allowed from time to time by law, and\nall usual and customary charges, costs and\nexpenses ;\n\n(m) to support and subscribe to any charitable or\npublic object and to any institution, society\nor cluo which may be for the benefit of the\ncompany or its employees or may be\nconnected with any town or place where\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                              7\n\nthe company carries on business; to give\npensions, gratuities or charitable aid to\nany person or persons who may serve or\nhave served the company or to the wives,\nchildren or other relatives of such persons;\nto make payments towards insurance and\n\nto form and contribute to provident and .\n\nbenefit funds for the benefit of any persons\nemployed by the company:\n\nProvided that no such subscription, gift,\n\n(n) to\n\n(0) to\n\n(p) to\n\npayment or contribution shall be given or\nmade, except out of profits of the company\navailable for distribution as dividend;\n\ncarry on in the Colony and the State of\nBrunei or in either of them, but not else-\n\n\"where except in so far as may be incidental\n\nto and necessary for the proper per-\nformance of the duties of any office\nheld by the company in the Federation,\nthe Colony, or the State of Brunei,\nany business or to hold any office which a\ntrust company is by this Ordinance\nauthorised to carry on or to hold in the\nFederation ;\n\nacquire and undertake the whole or any\npart of the business of any person or\ncompany of a like nature to any business\nwhich a trust company is authorised to\ncarry on, and in consideration for such\nacquisition to undertake all or any of the\nliabilities of such person or company and.\nto issue shares to such person or company;\n\ndo all such other things as are incidental\nor conducive to the attainment of the\naforementioned objects or any of them.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section shall be construed to\nauthorise any trust company to engage in the business\nof banking, or of insurance, or of life assurance within\nthe meaning of the Life Assurance Companies Ordin-\nance, 1948, or the business of a deposit, provident or\nbenefit society.\n\n(3) No trust company shall carry on any business\nor execute any office other than the businesses or offices\nincluded in the objects set out in sub-section (1) of\nthis section.\n\nTo carry on\n\nbusiness in\n\nthe Colony.\n\nTo acquire\nother\nbusinesses.\n\nTo do things\n\nconducive\nto objects.\n\nF.M. Ord.\nNo. 38 of\n1948,\n\nCompany\nmay act as\nexecutor.\n\nCompany\nmay be\nauthorised\nto apply for\nprobate or\nadministra\ntion.\n\n8             No. 83 or 1949.\n\nPROBATE AND ADMINISTRATION.\n\n9, If at any time a trust company is appointed\nexecutor of the will of any testator, it shall be lawful\nfor the company to apply to the Court for probate of\nthe will and, if probate be granted, to exercise and\ndischarge all the powers and duties of an executor."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"en":"10. (1) If and whenever any person is entitled to\napply for probate of the will of any testator without\nleave being reserved to any other person to apply for\nprobate, it shall be lawful for such person, whether\nabsent from the Federation or not, and notwithstand-\ning the provisions of any other written law, instead of\nhimself applying for such probate, to authorise a trust\ncompany to apply to the Court for a grant of adminis-\ntration with the will annexed of the estate of such\ntestator, and such grant may be made to the company\nupon its own application, when so authorised, but the\nprovisions of this section shall not apply to any case\nin which a will provides that the company shall not\nact as executor, or in the trusts thereof.\n\n(2) If and whenever any person is entitled to apply\nfor letters of administration with the will of any\ntestator annexed of the estate of such testator, it shall\nbe lawful for such person, whether absent from the\nFederation or not and notwithstanding the provisions\nof any other written law, to authorise a trust\ncompany, either alone or jointly with .any other\nperson, to apply to the Court for a grant of letters of\nadministration with the will annexed of the estate of\nsuch testator, and such grant may be made to the\ncompany upon its own application, when so autho-\nrised, but the provisions of this section shall not apply\nto a case in which a will provides that the company\nshall not act as executor, or in the trusts thereof.\n\n(3) It shall be lawful for any person or persons\nentitled to apply for letters of administration of the\nestate of dny intestate, whether such person or persons\nbe absent from the Federation or not, and notwith-\nstanding the provisions of any other written law, to\nauthorise a trust company to apply to the Court for\nsuch letters of administration, either alone or jointly\nwith any other person, and administration of the\nestate of any such intestate may be granted to the\ncompany, either alone or jointly as aforesaid, upon its\nown application, when so authorised.\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                            9\n\n(4) For the purposes of any application to the Court\nfor letters of administration to the estate of any\ndeceased person, the Court shall consider a trust\ncompany, when authorised as aforesaid, to be in law\nentitled equally with any other person or class\nof persons to apply for and obtain a grant, but a trust\ncompany, being so entitled, shall not on that account\nalone be preferred to the widower, widow, or\nnext-of-kin of any intestate.\n\n(5) No grant of probate or of letters of administra-\ntion shall be granted to a syndic or nominee on behalf\nof a trust company.               ,"}},{"id":"MY-H135-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"en":"11. (1) In all cases in which a trust company\nis empowered under this Ordinance to apply for\nprobate or for letters of administration, any petition,\ndeclaration, account or affidavit or other necessary\ndocument may be made or sworn by any officer of the\ncompany duly authorised by the company in that\nbehalf.\n\n_ (2) Any officer of the company appointed by the\ncompany for that purpose may, on behalf of the\ncompany, sign any petition, account or statement, take\nany oath, swear any affidavit, make any declaration,\nverify any act, give personal attendance at any Court\nor place, and do any act or thing whatsoever, which\nmay be required to be signed, taken, sworn, made,\nverified, given, or done on behalf of the company :\n\nProvided always that nothing in this Ordinance\ncontained shall confer upon any person, not otherwise\nentitled thereto, any right to appear or be heard before\nor in any Court on behalf of the company or to do any\nact whatsoever on behalf of the compdny which could\notherwise be lawfully done only by an advocate and\nsolicitor of the Court.\n\nTRUSTEESHIP."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"en":"12. In all cases in which the Court or any person or\npersons has or have power to appoint a trustee,\nwhether as an original or new or additional trustee,\nto perform any legal trust or duty, a trust company\nmay be appointed in the same manner as if the\ncompany were a private individual :\n\nProvided that no trust company shall be appointed\nin any case in which the instrument creating the trust,\nor the power authorising the appointment, forbids the\nappointment of a company.\n\nProcedure\nas to peti-\ntions, etc.\n\nAppoint-\nment of\ncompany\nto be\ntrustee.\n\nJoint\ntenancy\n\nCompany\nmay act as\nagent.\n\nTrust com-\npany not to\nfurnish\nsecurity.\n\nTrust funds\nto be kept\nseparate.\n\n10            No. 33 oF 1949."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"en":"13. A trust company, acting in a fiduciary capacity,\nshall be capable of acquiring and holding any property\nin joint tenancy in the same manner as if it were a\nprivate individual.\n\nAGENCY."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"en":"14. It shall be lawful for a trust company to act\nunder any deed or instrument by which the company\nis appointed agent or attorney for any person, and all\nthe powers conferred upon the company by any such\ndeed or instrument may be exercised by such officer of\nthe company as the company may appoint for that\npurpose :\n\nProvided that nothing in this section shall be\ndeemed to authorise any person to confer upon a trust\ncompany any power which may not lawfully be\n\ndelegated by him.\n\nEXEMPTION FROM GIVING SECURITY."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"text":{"en":"15. (1) Notwithstanding the provisions of any writ-\nten law for the time being in force relating to the\nadministration of estates of deceased persons a trust\ncompany to which a grant of letters of administration\nhas been made shall not be required to furnish security\nfor the due administration of the estate.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the provisions of any written\nlaw for the time being in force, a trust company\nappointed by the Court to perform the duties of\nreceiver, guardian, committee, or any other office or\ntrust shall not be required to furnish security for the\ndue performance of such duties.\n\nINVESTMENT OF TRUST FUNDS."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"text":{"en":"16. All moneys, property and securities recéived or\nheld by: any trust company in a fiduciary capacity\nshall always be kept distinct from those of the\ncompany, and in separate accounts, and shall be so\nmarked in the books of the company relating to each\nparticular trust as always to be distinguished from\nany other in the registers and other books of account\nkept by the company, so that at no time shall trust\nmoneys form part of or be mixed with the general as-\nsets of the company, and all investments made by the\ncompany as trustee shall be so designated that\nthe trusts to which such investments belong can be\nreadily identified at any time.\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                          11"}},{"id":"MY-H135-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"text":{"en":"17. (1) A trust company may invest trust moneys\nin its hands in or upon any securities in which private\ntrustees may by law invest trust moneys, and may\nfrom time to time vary any such investment for others\nof the same nature:\n\nProvided that the company shall not in any case\ninvest the moneys of any trust in or upon securities\nprohibited by the instrument creating the trust, and\nwhenever any special directions are given in any\norder, judgment, decree, or will, or in any other\ninstrument creating the trust, as to the particular\nclass or kind of securities or property in or upon which\nany investment shall be made, the company shall\nfollow such directions.\n\nThe company may also, in its discretion, retain and\ncontinue any investment and securities coming into\nits possession in.any fiduciary capacity.\n\n(2) No trust company shall directly or indirectly\ninvest any trust moneys otherwise than in accordance\nwith the provisions of sub-section (1) of this section.\n\nINVESTMENT OF COMPANY'S FUNDS."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"text":{"en":"18. (1) A trust company may invest moneys\nforming part of its own capital or reserve or accumu-\nlated profits—\n\n(a) in or upon any securities in or upon which\nprivate trustees may by law invest trust\nmoneys, and\n\n(6) in or upon such other securities as the\nFinancial Secretary may from time to time\napprove.\n\n(2) A trust company may acquire and hold\nimmovable property for the actual use and occupation\nof itself or of any of its officers or servants, and may\nsell and dispose of the same.\n\n(3) A trust company may, for the protection of its\ninvestments, acquire land which hag been mortgaged\nto it, but shall sell any land so acquired within three\nyears after the acquisition thereof, unless such time\nis extended by the Financial Secretary.\n\n(4) No trust company shall directly or indirectly\ninvest any of its moneys otherwise than in accordance\nwith sub-sections (1), (2) and (8) of this section:\n\nProvided that nothing .in this section shall be\ndeemed to prevent the acceptance by a trust company\nof any securities whatsoever to secure the payment of\na debt previously contracted in good faith; but any\n\nInvestment\nof trust\nfunds.\n\nInvestment\n-of company's\nfunds.\n\nLoans to\ncompany's\nofficers\n\nprohibited.\n\nBorrowing.\n\nAnnual\n\nStatement.\n\n12            No. 38 or 1949.\n\nsecurity so acquired by the company which it would\notherwise be prohibited from taking or holding shall,\nwithin two years from the time of its acquisition, or\nwithin such further time as may be allowed by .the\nRegistrar, be sold or disposed of."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"text":{"en":"19. No loan shall be made by any trust company\nto any director or other officer or servant thereof, or\nto any company or firm in the management of which\nany such director or other officer or servant is\nactively engaged.\n\nBORROWING POWER."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"text":{"en":"20. (1) For the purpose of attaining the objects of\nthe company as set out in section 8 of this Ordinance\n(or such of them as the company may have adopted),\nand for no other purpose, a trust company may frora\ntime to time borrow money:\n\nProvided that the aggregate of the sums of money\nborrowed shall not at any time exceed the amount of\nthe company's capital for the time being paid up.\n\n(2) Moneys borrowed by a trust company shall not\nbe secured, by debenture or otherwise, on its capital\nor general undertaking, but may be sécured on -any\nof the company's property (not being property held\nby it on any trust), other than the securities deposited\nby it with the Accountant-General under the provi-\nsions of this Ordinance.\n\nANNUAL STATEMENT."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"text":{"en":"21. (1) Every trust company shall forward annually\nto the Registrar, together with the list of members\nand summary required by section 109 of the Companies\nOrdinance, or, in the case of a company incorporated\nin the Colony, with the balance sheet required by\nsection 303 of the Companies Ordinance, a statement\nof the liabilities of the company to the public in its\ntrustee capacity, and of the investments and holdings\nof the company on trust account.\n\n(2) The statement shall be verified by the affidavit\nof the chairman or vice-chairman and of the manager\nor secretary of the company.\n\n(3) Every document purporting to be certified by\nthe Registrar to be a copy of any such statement or of\npart thereof shall be deemed to be a copy of that\nstatement or of part thereof, and shall be received in\nevidence as if it were the original statement or part\nthereof, unless some variation between it and the\noriginal statement is proved.\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                          13\n\nINSPECTION."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"text":{"en":"22. (1) The High Commissioner may at any time\nappoint an inspector to investigate the affairs and\nmanagement of any trust company and may prescribe\nthe manner in, and the extent to, which the investiga-\ntion shall be conducted.\n\n(2) It shall be the duty of all officers and servants of\nthe company to produce for examination by the inspec-\ntor all books, accounts, vouchers and other documents\nin their custody or control in relation to the matters\nunder investigation, and to answer truly all inquiries\naddressed to them by(the inspector respecting any\nmatter affecting the affairs of the company.\n\n(3) The inspector shall make a report of his investi-\ngation to the Financial Secretary.\n\n(4) All expenses of and incidental to any investiga-\ntion shall be paid by the company, if the Financial\nSecretary so directs.\n\nWINDING UP."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"text":{"en":"23. The Court may order the winding up of a trust\ncompany in accordance with the Companies Ordinance\nand the provisions of that Ordinance shall apply\naccordingly, subject, however, to the modification that\nthe company may be ordered to be wound up on\napplication made by or on behalf of the Financial\nSecretary showing—\n\n(a) that the company has made default in com-\nplying with a requirement of this Ordi-\nnance and such default has continued for a\nperiod of two months after notice of\ndefault has been served upon the company;\nor\n\n(6) that from the consideration of the report of\nan inspector appointed under section 22 of\nthis Ordinance it appears to him that the\n\ncompany is insolvent or has committed a:\n\nbreach of trust.\n\nLIABILITY OF OFFICERS."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"text":{"en":"24. Where a trust company holds the office of\nexecutor, administrator or trustee, every person\nemployed by the company to discharge any of the\nduties of such office shall, in respect of the duties\nentrusted to him, be personally responsible to the Court\nand be subject to the process of the Court, as though\nhe had been personally appointed to such office.\n\nInvestiga-\ntion by\ninspector.\n\nSpecial pro-\nvision as to\nwinding-up.\n\nPersonal\nliability\nof officers.\n\nLoan to\ndirector,\netc.\n\nLiability on\nwinding up.\n\nWilful\nneglect\nto make\nentry.\n\nFalse\nstatements\nin accounts.\n\nRefusal to\nproduce\nbooks.\n\nNeglect to\nforward\nannual\nstatement,\n\nNo. 33 or 1949."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"text":{"en":"25. If any loan is made by a trust company to any\ndirector or other officer or servant thereof in contra-\nvention of section 19 of this-Ordinance, all directors\nand officers of the company who made the loan or\nassented thereto shall be jointly and severally liable\nto the company for the amount thereof with interest."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"text":{"en":"26. Upon the winding up of a trust company, every\nperson who has been a director of the company at any\ntime within the period of two years immediately\npreceding the commencement of the winding up shall\nbecome liable for the balance unpaid on every share\nwhich he may have transferred during such two years.\n\nPENALTIES."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"text":{"en":"27. Any director, officer or servant of a trust\ncompany who wilfully and with intent to defraud\nneglects to make any entry in the books of the company\nwhich it is his duty to make shall be guilty of an\noffence, and shall be liable to imprisonment of either\ndescription for a term not exceeding two years."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"text":{"en":"28. Any director, officer or servant of a trust\ncompany who wilfully and with intent to defraud\nmakes or abets the making of any false entry in the\nbooks of the company or subscribes or exhibits any false\ndocument with intent to deceive any person appointed\nunder this Ordinance to investigate the affairs and\nmanagement of the company shall be guilty of an\noffence, and shall be liable to imprisonment of either\ndescription for a term not exceeding two years."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"text":{"en":"29. Any director, officer or servant of a trust\ncompany who refuses to produce for examination to\nany person appointed under this Ordinance to inves-\ntigate the affairs and management of the company all\nbooks and documents relevant to such investigation\nwhich are in his custody or control shall be liable to\nimprisonment of either description for a term not\nexceeding twelve months, or to a fine not exceeding\nfive hundred dollars, or to both such imprisonment\nand fine."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"text":{"en":"30. Any trust company which makes default in\nforwarding to the Registrar the verified statement as\nrequired by section 21 of this Ordinance shall be liable\nto a fine not exceeding fifty dollars for every day\nduring which the default continues, in addition to any\npenalty which it may incur under the Companies\nOrdinance, and any director or manager of the\ncompany who knowingly and wilfully authorises or\npermits the default shall be liable to the like penalty.\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.\n\nGENERAL."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"text":{"en":"31. No trust company shall be appointed to be\nguardian of the person of an infant or committee of\nthe person of a mentally disordered person."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"text":{"en":"32. No member of a trust company shall at any time\nhold, or have any interest in shares in the capital of\nthe company to an amount exceeding one fifth of the\nissued capital of the company for the time being."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"text":{"en":"33. So long as any estate in respect of which a trust\ncompany is trustee shall remain in whole or in part\nunadministered, it shall not be lawful to proceed to\nwind up the company voluntarily, unless with the\nsanction of the Court, and it shall be lawful for any\nperson interested in such estate, or who may have any\nclaim in respect thereof, to apply to the Court in a\nsummary way by motion to restrain any director or\nany shareholder from disposing of any shares which\nsuch director or shareholder may hold in the company\nor to restrain the voluntary winding up of the\ncompany, and the Court shall have power to make\nsuch order as it deems just."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34"},"text":{"en":"34. Subject to the provisions of this Ordinance, the\nliability of every trust company to the person or\npersons interested in any estate held by the company\nas executor, administrator, trustee, receiver, liqui-\ndator, assignee, guardian, or committee, or in any\nother official or business capacity shall be the same as\nif the estate had been held by a private person in the\nlike capacity and the powers of the company shall be\nthe same as those of a private person in the like\ncapacity."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35"},"text":{"en":"35. Neither the application by a trust company for\nregistration as a member or shareholder in the books\nof any company or corporation nor the entry of the\nname of a trust company in the books of any company\nor corporation shall constitute notice of trust, and no\ncompany or corporation shall be entitled to object to\nenter the name of a trust company on its books by\nreason only that the company may be or is a trustee,\nand, in dealings with property, the fact that the\nperson or one of the persons dealt with is a trust com-\npany shall not of itself constitute notice of a trust."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36"},"text":{"en":"36. All money and securities which shall remain in\nthe hands of a trust company, as trustee, unclaimed\nby the person entitled to the same for a period of six\n\nGuardian-\nship of\nperson pro-\nhibited.\n\nRestriction\non holding\nof shares.\n\nVoluntary\nwinding up\nor disposal\nof shares\nmay be\nrestrained,\n\nLiability\nand powers\nof company.\n\nRegistration\nof trust\ncompany as\nshareholder,\netc., not\nnotice of a.\ntrust.\n\nUnclaimed\nmoney to be\npaid into\nCourt.\n\n7?\n\nFees.\n\nRepeal.\nS.S. Cap.\n\nM.U. Ord.\n\n13 of 1946.\n\n16            No. 33 oF 1949.\n\nyears after the time when the same shall have become\npayable to such person (except where payment has\nbeen restrained by order of a court of competent\njurisdiction), together with such interest, if any, as\nshall have been received by the company in respect\nthereof, less any commission or other charges properly\nchargeable by the company, shall be paid by the\ncompany into Court and shall be dealt with according\nto the orders of the Court :\n\nProvided that it shall not be necessary fbr the\ncompany to comply with the provisions of this section\nmore often than once in any year, nor shall it\nbe necessary for the company to obtain the concurrence\nor consent of any person to such payment into Court."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37"},"text":{"en":"37. (1) There shall be paid to the Registrar in -\nrespect of the matters mentioned in the Schedule\nto this Ordinance the several fees specified therein.\n\n(2) All such fees shall be paid by the Registrar to\nthe Accountant-General.\n\n(3) The High Commissioner in Council may, from\ntime to time, by notification in the Gazette, add to,\nalter or amend the said Schedule."}},{"id":"MY-H135-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38"},"text":{"en":"38. The Trust Companies Ordinance of the Straits\nSettlements is hereby repealed :\n\nProvided that a company which was registered as\na trust company before the thirty-first day of\nDecember, 1941, under the provisions of the Ordin-\nance hereby repealed and which is registered as\nincorporated in the Federation in pursuance of the\nCompanies Ordinance, 1946, shall, on application\nmade to the Registrar in that behalf and on the\nRegistrar being satisfied—\n\n(a) that the securities already deposited by such\ncompany under the provisions of such\nrepealed Ordinance have been transferred\nto and are duly deposited with the\nAccountant-General; and\n\n(>) that such securities are of the value of at least\none hundred thousand dollars,\n\nbe entitled, without payment of any fee in respect\nthereof, to be registered as a trust company under\nsection 4 of this Ordinance and to be issued with\na certificate of registration in accordance with\nthe provisions of that section.\n\nTRUST COMPANIES.                          17\n\nTHE SCHEDULE.\n(Section 87.)\nFEES TO BE PAID TO THE REGISTRAR."}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1350"] = {"id":"MY-H1350","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2022&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2022年供应管制（管制物品）（第2号）（修正）令","en":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 2) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022","orig":"CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 2) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022","ms":"Perintah Kawalan Bekalan (Barang Kawalan) (Bilangan 2) (Pindaan) 2022","vi":"Lệnh về Kiểm soát nguồn cung (Hàng hóa được kiểm soát) (số 2) (Sửa đổi) năm 2022","th":"คำสั่งการควบคุมเสบียง (สิ่งของควบคุม) (ฉบับที่ 2) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2022","id":"Perintah Pengendalian Persediaan (Barang yang Dikendalikan) (Nomor 2) (Perubahan) Tahun 2022"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2022","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2022_P.U.(A)143-2022_CONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 2) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1350-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kawalan Bekalan\n\n(Barang-Barang Kawalan) (No. 2) (Pindaan) 2022.\n\nPindaan perenggan 2"}},{"id":"MY-H1350-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Kawalan Bekalan (Barang-Barang Kawalan) (No. 2) 2022\n\n[P.U. (A) 120/2022] dipinda dalam perenggan 2 dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"6 Mei 2022\" dengan perkataan \"10 Mei 2022\".\n\nDibuat 27 April 2022\n\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)0.5001/4 Jld. 8; PN(PU2)188/Jld. 13]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMenteri Perdagangan Dalam Negeri dan Hal Ehwal Pengguna\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES ACT 1961\n\nCONTROL OF SUPPLIES (CONTROLLED ARTICLES) (NO. 2)\n\n(AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 5 of the\n\nControl of Supplies Act 1961 [Act 122], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
  FT["MY-H1351"] = {"id":"MY-H1351","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 143/2023&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2023年道路交通（禁止使用道路）（联邦道路）（第10号）令","en":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2023","orig":"ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2023","ms":"Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Persekutuan) (Bilangan 10) 2023","vi":"Lệnh về Vận tải đường bộ (Cấm sử dụng đường bộ) (Đường bộ liên bang) (số 10) năm 2023","th":"คำสั่งการขนส่งทางถนน (การห้ามใช้ถนน) (ทางหลวงสหพันธ์) (ฉบับที่ 10) ค.ศ. 2023","id":"Perintah Angkutan Jalan (Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Raya Federal) (Nomor 10) Tahun 2023"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA143","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2023","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2023_P.U.(A)143-2023_ROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2023.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H1351-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pengangkutan Jalan\n\n(Larangan Penggunaan Jalan) (Jalan Persekutuan) (No. 10) 2023.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 8 Mei 2023.\n\nLarangan"}},{"id":"MY-H1351-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Pemanduan kenderaan di atas bahagian jalan yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1)\n\nJadual Pertama sebagaimana yang ditunjukkan dalam peta dalam Jadual Kedua,\n\nmelainkan di atas jalan arah yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (2) Jadual Pertama,\n\nbagi tempoh yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (3) Jadual Pertama, dilarang.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n(1)\n\nJalan yang baginya\n\nLarangan Terpakai\n\n(2)\n\nJalan Arah\n\n(3)\n\nTempoh Larangan\n\nSebahagian Laluan 64,\n\nJalan Maran-Jerantut–Benta\n\nbermula dari seksyen 35.00\n\nhingga seksyen 35.20\n\nsebagaimana yang\n\nditunjukkan dalam peta\n\ndalam Jadual Kedua\n\nKenderaan dari Benta ke\n\nJerantut/Maran dan sebaliknya\n\nhendaklah menggunakan jalan\n\nalternatif sebagaimana yang\n\nditunjukkan dalam peta dalam\n\nJadual Kedua\n\n8 Mei 2023 hingga\n\n31 Januari 2024\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\nDibuat 3 Mei 2023\n\n[KKR.100-1/2/79 Jld.5; PN(PU2)460/Jld. 124]\n\n DATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\n Menteri Kerja Raya\n\nROAD TRANSPORT ACT 1987\n\nROAD TRANSPORT (PROHIBITION OF USE OF ROAD)\n\n(FEDERAL ROADS) (NO. 10) ORDER 2023\n\nWHEREAS by P.U. (B) 129/2023 published on 6 April 2023,\n\nnotice was given of the intention to make an order under section 70\n\nof the Road Transport Act 1987 [Act 333]:\n\nAND WHEREAS no objection was received by the Minister of Works against the making\n\nof such order:\n\nNOW THEREFORE, in exercise of the powers conferred by section 70 of the Act,\n\nthe Minister of Works, after taking into consideration the matters referred to in\n\nsubsection 70(2) of the Act, makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Road Transport (Prohibition of Use\n\nof Road) (Federal Roads) (No. 10) Order 2023.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 8 May 2023.\n\nProhibition\n\n2. The driving of vehicles on the part of the road as specified in column (1)\n\nof the First Schedule as shown on the map in the Second Schedule, otherwise than on the\n\nroutes specified in column (2) of the First Schedule, for the period specified in column (3)\n\nof the First Schedule, is prohibited.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n(1)\n\nRoad to which\n\nProhibition Applies\n\n(2)\n\nRoutes\n\n(3)\n\nProhibition Period\n\nPart of Route 64,\n\nMaran-Jerantut–Benta Road\n\nstarting from section 35.00 to\n\nsection 35.20 as shown on the\n\nmap in the Second Schedule\n\nVehicles from Benta\n\nto Jerantut/Maran and\n\nvice versa shall use the\n\nalternative road as shown on\n\nthe map in the Second\n\nSchedule\n\n8 May 2023 to\n\n31 January 2024\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\nMade 3 May 2023\n\n[KKR.100-1/2/79 Jld.5; PN(PU2)460/Jld. 124]\n\n DATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\n Minister of Works"}}],"pack":"my-3"};
